hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19801","Ahmad ibn al-Khadir al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Abda al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'adh al-Nahwi al-Fadl ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Raqaba ibn Masqala, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at al-Abtah in a tent of leather. Bilal came out and called the adhan for the prayer, the noon prayer; then he entered and performed his ablution for him, then brought out the remainder of his ablution water in a basin, and we crowded over it — some obtaining in full, some being sprinkled with what was decreed for him of the water. Then he entered and brought out an 'anaza and fixed it between himself and the qibla, with women and donkeys passing. Then he announced the prayer, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out in a red hulla, as if I am looking at the gleam of his shins, and led us in noon and afternoon as two rak'as each."
"19802","Ishaq ibn Jamil al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying at al-Abtah, with an 'anaza fixed before him, while donkeys and women passed in front of him."
"19803","Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Banna' al-Kufi narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Murri narrated to us, Bassam al-Sayrafi narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a red tent of leather. Bilal brought out the remainder of his ablution water, and the people vied for it — some taking something, some taking nothing. Then Bilal brought out an 'anaza and fixed it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and prayed toward it, while people and animals passed in front of him."
"19804","'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' al-Kufi narrated to us, (h) and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us — they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Abtah two rak'as, the afternoon prayer."
"19805","Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Wahb Abu Juhayfa, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Abtah pray the afternoon prayer as two rak'as."
"19806","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Umar Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray afternoon at al-Abtah as two rak'as, with an 'anaza placed before him between himself and passersby on the road."
"19807","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi and Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, (h) and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl al-Nakha'i narrated to us — they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfa: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered at Mina, an 'anaza was fixed, and he prayed toward it."
"19808","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us, (h) and Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (h) and Ibrahim ibn Sharik al-Asadi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us — they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — this part of him was white, and he pointed to his 'anfaqah. 'Amr ibn Khalid added in his hadith: It was said to him: Like whom were you in those days? He said: I used to strip arrows and feather them."
"19809","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with grayness in his 'anfaqah below his lower lip."
"19810","Muhammad ibn 'Abdaws ibn Kamil and Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shayba said: Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Salih, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, you have grown gray. He said: 'Hud and its sisters have made me gray.'"
"19811","Muhammad ibn 'Abdaws ibn Kamil and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting one day with people before him doing something he disliked of their talk and noise. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not forbid them? He said: 'Had I forbidden them from al-Hajun, one of them would soon come to it without need.'"
"19812","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, (h) and 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, (h) and Abu Khalifa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us — they said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, who said: I heard Abu Juhayfa say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out at midday; ablution water was brought and he performed ablution. People took from the remainder of his purification water and wiped themselves with it. He prayed noon as two rak'as and afternoon as two rak'as, with an 'anaza before him. This is the wording of the hadith of 'Asim ibn 'Ali; the others are similar."
"19813","'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and Ishaq ibn Jamil al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Daqiqi narrated to us — they said: Yazid ibn Harun and Sufyan ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Juhayfa: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped at al-Abtah. I went out among those who looked at him and saw him brought ablution water with which he performed ablution. Then he fixed an 'anaza and prayed with his Companions two rak'as when the sun had passed its zenith."
"19814","'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Abu Isra'il narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, set prices for us. He said: 'Allah is the Price-Setter, the Withholder, the Extender. I hope to meet Allah with none of you seeking from me any redress for an honor or wealth.'"
"19815","'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Qatan ibn Nusayr al-Dari' narrated to us, Yazid Abu Khalid al-Baysari narrated to us, Abu Malik informed us, Salama ibn Kuhayl informed me, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Sit with the scholars, question the elders, and mix with the wise.'"
"19816","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Talq ibn Ghannam narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Sit with the elders, question the scholars, and mix with the wise.'"
"19817","'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Qabisa narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Ibn Abjar, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, who said: Abu Juhayfa met me and said: O Salama, nothing remains of what I used to know except this prayer, and there is no soul whose death would please me as a shield — not even the soul of a fly."
"19818","'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Khalid, from Wahb al-Suwa'i, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I was sent, I and the Hour, like this one of this' — as though it would almost precede me."
"19819","'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Kufi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, 'Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Raja', from Abu Juhayfa, who said: I belched in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: 'What did you eat, O Abu Juhayfa?' I said: Bread and meat. He said: 'The longest in hunger on the Day of Resurrection will be those most satiated in this world.'"
"19820","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Amr al-Ash'athi narrated to us, (h) and 'Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us — both said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiya al-Fazari narrated to us, Salih ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) white, with gray in his sideburns."
"19821","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Amr al-Ash'athi narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiya narrated to us, Salih ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, Abu Juhayfa Wahb al-Suwa'i narrated to me, who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he wrote for us twelve young she-camels. When he passed away, the people withheld them from us until they gathered."
"19822","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym Dirar ibn Surad and Wasil ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) white, having grown gray. Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali resembled him. He ordered for us twelve young she-camels; we went to collect them but came upon his death, and they gave us nothing. When Abu Bakr took charge, he said: Whoever has a promise from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him come. I informed him, and he ordered them for us."
"19823","'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and al-Hasan ibn 'Ali resembled him."
"19824","Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, who said: I said to Abu Juhayfa: Did you see the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: 'Yes, and al-Hasan resembles him.'"
"19825","Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and al-Hasan resembled him."
"19826","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I walked with Abu Juhayfa to Friday prayer and said: Did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: 'Yes, and al-Hasan ibn 'Ali was likened to him.'"
"19827","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Wahb Abu Juhayfa — I said: Did you see the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: 'Yes, and al-Hasan ibn 'Ali resembled him.'"
"19828","Maslama ibn Ahmad al-Ghawri al-Himsi said: My maternal grandfather Khattab ibn 'Uthman narrated to me, he said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'There is no servant or maidservant who refrains from walking to fulfill the need of his Muslim brother but walks the like of it in the wrath of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; nor refrains from spending an expenditure in the path of Allah but spends manifold multiples in the wrath of Allah; nor leaves Hajj for some worldly purpose but sees those left behind before he fulfills that need.'"
"19829","al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, 'Ubayd ibn Ya'ish narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn 'Adi narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought a garment from the fuller, or taken to the fuller, upon which was written 'devil,' and he ordered that it be erased, saying: 'I seek refuge in Allah from Satan.' 'Ubayd ibn Ya'ish raised it as a prophetic hadith, while others reported it as a Companion's statement."
"19830","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn 'Adi narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, who said: Abu Juhayfa saw me with a garment I was taking to the fuller, upon which was written 'devil,' and he forbade me — and this is the correct version."
"19831","Zakariyya al-Saji, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami, and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari said: Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Kathir, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: I was told that the people of a household follow one another into the Fire until none remains of them — neither free, nor slave, nor maidservant — and that the people of a household follow one another into Paradise until none remains of them — neither free, nor slave, nor maidservant."
"19832","'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, who said: I heard Abu Juhayfa say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I do not eat reclining.'"
"19833","'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfa: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I do not eat reclining.'"
"19834","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Mis'ar and Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I do not eat reclining.'"
"19835","'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, who said: Abu Juhayfa informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I do not eat reclining.'"
"19836","'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to me, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, Sufyan informed me, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I do not eat reclining.'"
"19837","'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani, and Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, (h) and Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, Yahya al-Himmani, and 'Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us — they said: Sharik narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'I do not eat reclining.'"
"19838","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad said: Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from Mansur and Raqaba ibn Masqala, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'As for me, I do not eat reclining.'"
"19839","Ishaq ibn Jamil al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, 'Abida ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Mansur, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'I do not eat reclining.'"
"19840","Abu Zur'a 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Adam narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I do not eat reclining.'"
"19841","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar narrated to me, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I do not eat reclining.'"
"19842","'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu al-Sha'tha' 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Za'ida, from Mansur, from Kulthum ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man with him: 'I do not eat reclining.'"
"19843","'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Rabi'a Fahd ibn 'Awf narrated to us, a shaykh of ours called al-Fadl ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Musa informed me, he said: I am 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: I ate a tharid of wheat bread with fatty meat, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and kept belching. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Restrain your belching, for those most satiated in this world will be the hungriest in the Hereafter.'"
"19844","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Sa'dan ibn Nasr al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Abu Qatada al-Harrani narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray until his feet swelled. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed. He said: 'Shall I not be a grateful servant?'"
"19845","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, Mahbub ibn Muhriz al-Qawariri narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Nakha'i, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfa: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man who had let his garment hang loose in prayer, and he drew it together for him."
"19846","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: 'Sit with the elders, mix with the wise, and question the scholars.'"
"19847","Abu Zur'a 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, (h) and 'Amr ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, (h) and 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us — they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu 'Umar, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: Riches were mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Some said: My grandfather's wealth is in horses; some said: My grandfather's wealth is in camels; some said: My grandfather's wealth is in sheep. Prayer came, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them. When he raised his head from bowing, he said: 'Allah hears whoever praises Him; our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth, and filling whatever You will beyond that. None withholds what You give, none gives what You withhold, none repels what You decree, and the wealth of the wealthy avails him nothing before You.'"
"19848","'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu 'Umar, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of his neighbor, and he said: 'Throw your belongings onto the road.' He threw them, and people began passing by him and cursing him. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what I suffered from the people! He said: 'And what did you suffer from them?' He said: They curse me. He said: 'Allah cursed you before the people.' He said: I shall not repeat it. The one who had complained came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to him: 'Lift your belongings; you have been sufficed.'"
"19849","'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir and Bayan, from al-Sha'bi, from Wahb ibn Khanbash, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'An 'umra in Ramadan equals a Hajj.'"
"19850","Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Wahb ibn Khanbash, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'An 'umra in Ramadan equals a Hajj.'"
"19851","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, (h) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Kathir ibn Yahya Abu Malik, the companion of al-Basri, narrated to us — both said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi' ibn Habban, from Wahb ibn Hudhayfa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'When a man rises from his seat then returns to it, he has most right to it.'"
"19852","Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Bazzar and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari said: Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Dukayn, from Wahb ibn Hamza, who said: I accompanied 'Ali from Medina to Mecca and saw from him some of what I disliked. I said: If I return to the Messenger of Allah, I shall complain of you to him. When I arrived, I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I saw such-and-such from 'Ali. He said: 'Do not say this, for he is the worthiest of people in authority over you after me.'"
"19853","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hawbar ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud al-Harrani narrated to us, Wahshi ibn Harb ibn Wahshi ibn Harb narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: When the Negus died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Your brother the Negus has died; stand and pray over him.' A man said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall we pray over him when he died in disbelief? He said: 'Have you not heard the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: And indeed, among the People of the Book are those who believe in Allah and in what was sent down to you and what was sent down to them — to the end of the verse.'"
"19854","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hawbar ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Wahshi ibn Harb ibn Wahshi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather: that when Allah granted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Safiyya as spoil, he said to his Companions: 'What do you say about this slave girl?' They said: You are the worthiest of people of her and most entitled. He said: 'I have freed her and taken her in marriage, making her freedom her dowry.' A man said: O Messenger of Allah, the wedding feast? He said: 'The wedding feast is a duty; the second is kindness; the third is boasting and burden.'"
"19855","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hawbar ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Wahshi ibn Harb narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken by night into Paradise, he heard a rustling sound and said: 'O Jibril, what is this rustling?' He said: This is Bilal. Abu Bakr said: 'Would that Bilal's mother had borne me and Bilal's father, and I were like Bilal.'"
"19856","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hawbar ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Wahshi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out at night for his need, leaving the door of the house open. Then he returned and found Iblis standing in the middle of the house. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Away with you, O wicked one, from my house.' Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'When you leave your houses at night, close their doors.'"
"19857","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Zayd al-Khattabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, Wahshi ibn Harb ibn Wahshi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Knowledge is about to be snatched away from people until you can grasp nothing of it.' Ziyad ibn Labid said: How is knowledge snatched from us when we have recited the Qur'an and taught it to our children? He said: 'May your mother be bereaved of you, O Ibn Labid — this Torah and Gospel are in the hands of the Jews and Christians, yet they pay no heed to them.'"
"19858","Abu 'Ubayda 'Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-'Askari narrated to us, Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Himsi al-Zubaydi, (h) and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Zayd al-Khattabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us — both said: Wahshi ibn Harb narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that he was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man passed, with another man sitting at the Prophet's side, who said: O Messenger of Allah, I love him for Allah's sake. He said: 'Have you told him so?' He said: No. He said: 'Stand and tell him.'"
"19859","Musa ibn 'Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, Sadaqa ibn Khalid narrated to us, (h) and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Zayd al-Khattabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us — both said: Wahshi ibn Harb ibn Wahshi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Perhaps after me you will conquer great cities and take seats in their markets. When that happens, return greetings, lower your gaze, guide the blind, and aid the wronged.'"
"19860","Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub al-Ahwazi narrated to us, 'Ali ibn 'Umar narrated to us — both said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Wahshi ibn Harb ibn Wahshi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Messenger of Allah, we eat but are not satisfied. He said: 'Perhaps you eat separately?' They said: Yes. He said: 'Gather over your food and mention the name of Allah over it; it will be blessed for you.'"
"19861","Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Baqi al-Adhani narrated to us, al-Musayyab ibn Wadih narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hurayra al-Himsi narrated to us, Wahshi ibn Harb ibn Wahshi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: When I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after the killing of Hamza, he spat in my face three times, then said: 'Do not show me your face.'"
"19862","Musa ibn 'Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, Sadaqa ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Wahshi ibn Harb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: 'Wahshi?' I said: Yes. He said: 'Did you kill Hamza?' I said: Yes — and praise be to Allah who honored him by my hand and did not disgrace me by his hands. Quraysh said to him: Do we love him while he is the killer of Hamza? I said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me. He spat on the ground three times, pushed my chest three times, and said: 'O Wahshi, go out and fight in the path of Allah as you fought to turn away from the path of Allah.'"
"19863","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, (h) and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, (h) and 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us — they said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Murra informed me, he said: I heard Hilal ibn Yasaf narrating from 'Amr ibn Rashid, from Wabisa ibn Ma'bad: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying alone in the row and ordered him to repeat the prayer."
"19864","Abu Shu'ayb 'Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from 'Amr ibn Murra, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from 'Amr ibn Rashid, from Wabisa ibn Ma'bad, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying alone behind the rows and ordered him to repeat the prayer."
"19865","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Ishkab narrated to us, Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Dalani narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murra, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from 'Amr ibn Rashid, from Wabisa ibn Ma'bad, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned from prayer while a man was praying alone behind the rows, and ordered him to repeat his prayer."
"19866","Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Wasibah 374 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, Waki' narrated, from Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from his uncle Ubayd ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Wasibah: that a man prayed behind the row alone, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to repeat the prayer."
"19867","375 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated, Ma'mar and al-Thawri narrated, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Wasibah ibn Ma'bad, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying behind the people alone, so he ordered him and he repeated the prayer."
"19868","376 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, he said: Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd took my hand and made me stand before an old man in al-Raqqah called Wasibah ibn Ma'bad, and he said: A man prayed behind the rows alone, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to repeat."
"19869","377 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, Jarir narrated, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Wasibah: that a man prayed behind the rows alone, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to repeat the prayer."
"19870","378 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Husayn narrated, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, he said: Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd stood with me before Wasibah ibn Ma'bad, he said: This shaykh narrated to me while he hears: that a man prayed behind the rows, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him and he repeated the prayer."
"19871","379 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, Za'idah narrated, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd, he said: Wasibah ibn Ma'bad narrated to me: that he saw a man pray in a row behind the people, not praying with the rows, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to repeat the prayer."
"19872","380 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shabib al-Assal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah narrated, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd, he said: He took my hand and made me stand before a man called Wasibah ibn Ma'bad, and he said while he hears: This narrated to me that a man prayed behind the rows, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to repeat the prayer, so he repeated."
"19873","381 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Khalid narrated, Husayn narrated, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, he said: Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd took my hand and made me stand before an old man in al-Raqqah called Wasibah ibn Ma'bad al-Asadi, and he said: This narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying in a row alone, so he ordered him and he repeated the prayer."
"19874","382 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to me, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Sharik narrated, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Wasibah ibn Ma'bad: that a man prayed behind the rows alone, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to repeat the prayer."
"19875","383 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, both said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Shimr ibn Atiyyah, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Wasibah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man praying behind the row alone? He said: He repeats."
"19876","384 - Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah al-Kilabi narrated, from Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from his uncle Ubayd ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Wasibah ibn Ma'bad: that a man prayed behind the rows alone, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him and he repeated."
"19877","385 - Muhammad ibn Sa'dan al-Atayidi narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated, Yusuf ibn Kamil narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ubayd ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Wasibah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying behind the row alone, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."
"19878","386 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, with its chain, the like of it."
"19879","387 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed, he said: I heard al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrating from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Wasibah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying behind the row alone, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."
"19880","Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Wasibah 388 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ubayd ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Wasibah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying behind the row alone, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."
"19881","389 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us, Ali ibn Ma'bad ibn Shaddad al-Raqqi narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Mubashshir ibn Ubayd, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Fudayl, from Amr, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Wasibah ibn Ma'bad, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not take riding animals as pulpits."
"19882","And I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed the worst of these beasts of prey is the thu'al, meaning the fox."
"19883","390 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Wasibah ibn Ma'bad, he said: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a row alone, so when he finished he said: Repeat the prayer."
"19884","391 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated, al-Muharibi narrated, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Wasibah, and Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Mansur, from Salim, from Wasibah, he said: I prayed behind the row, so he ordered me and I repeated my prayer."
"19885","al-Sha'bi from Wasibah 392 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: We read to Muhammad ibn Hafs ibn Umar al-Muqri, Sahl ibn Amir al-Bajali narrated, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Wasibah, he said: A man prayed behind the row alone, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to repeat."
"19886","393 - And Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, al-Sari ibn Isma'il narrated, from al-Sha'bi, from Wasibah ibn Ma'bad: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying behind the row alone, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."
"19887","394 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, Malik ibn Su'ayr narrated, al-Sari ibn Isma'il narrated, from al-Sha'bi, from Wasibah ibn Ma'bad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished while a man was praying behind the people alone, so he said: O you who prays alone, will you not join a row and enter with them, or draw a man to you if space is tight for you; repeat your prayer, for you have no prayer."
"19888","Hanash ibn al-Mu'tamir from Wasibah 395 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Hanash ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Wasibah ibn Ma'bad: that a man prayed behind the row alone, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to repeat the prayer."
"19889","396 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated, Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated, Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Hanash ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Wasibah ibn Ma'bad, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon me praying behind the row alone, so he ordered me to repeat the prayer."
"19890","397 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Hanash ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Wasibah ibn Ma'bad, that a man prayed behind the row alone, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to repeat the prayer."
"19891","398 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated, Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Wasibah, and Ash'ath, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Wasibah, he said: I prayed in a row alone behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered me to repeat the prayer."
"19892","Rashid ibn Abi Rashid from Wasibah 399 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Muqaddami narrated, Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Ata al-Khurasani narrated, Talhah ibn Zayd narrated, from Rashid ibn Abi Rashid, he said: I heard Wasibah ibn Ma'bad saying: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about everything, until I asked him about the dirt that is in the nails, so he said: Leave what puts you in doubt for what does not put you in doubt."
"19893","400 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated, Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Ata narrated, Talhah ibn Zayd narrated, from Rashid ibn Abi Rashid, from Wasibah ibn Ma'bad, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he bowed in his prayer, if water were poured on his back it would settle."
"19894","401 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated, Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Ata narrated, Talhah ibn Zayd narrated, from Rashid ibn Abi Rashid, from Wasibah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering a sermon in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he said: Let the witness convey to the absent."
"19895","Abu Abd Allah Muhammad al-Asadi from Wasibah 402 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, (H) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, both said: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated, Abu Abd Allah Muhammad al-Asadi narrated to me that he heard Wasibah ibn Ma'bad, the Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about righteousness and sin, so he said: O Wasibah, you came to ask me about righteousness and sin? So I said: Yes, by the One Who sent you with the truth, it is indeed what I came to ask you about, he said: So righteousness is what your chest is at ease with, and sin is what pricks in your chest, even if people give you a ruling about it."
"19896","Ayyub ibn Abd Allah ibn Mikraz from Wasibah 403 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hayyan al-Sami narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from al-Zubayr Abu Abd al-Salam, from Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Mikraz, from Wasibah ibn Ma'bad al-Asadi, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I did not want to leave anything of righteousness and sin except that I ask him about it, so I came to him while he was among a group of Muslims around him, and I began stepping over them to draw near to him, so some of them rebuked me and said: Away from the Messenger of Allah, O Wasibah, so I said: I love to draw near to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave Wasibah, draw near to me O Wasibah, so he drew me near until I was before him, and he said: Shall you ask me or shall I inform you? So I said: No, rather you inform me, so he said: You came to ask about righteousness and sin, I said: Yes, so he gathered his fingers and began tapping with them on my chest, and said: Righteousness is what the soul is at rest with and the heart is at rest with, and sin is what pricks in the soul and wavers in the chest, even if people give you rulings however they give you."
"19897","404 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Warqa narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent al-Walid ibn Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt to Banu al-Mustaliq as a collector."
"19898","405 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruwasi narrated, Abu Bakr al-Dahiri Abd Allah ibn Hakim narrated, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Walid ibn Uqbah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed some people of Paradise will go to some people of the Fire and say: By what did you enter the Fire, for by Allah we entered Paradise only by what we learned from you? So they say: We used to say and not do."
"19899","406 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Fayyad ibn Muhammad al-Raqqi narrated, Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated, from Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj al-Kilabi, from Abd Allah al-Hamdani, from al-Walid ibn Uqbah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) opened Makkah, the people of Makkah began bringing their children to him, and he would wipe over their heads and supplicate for them, so I was brought to him while I was perfumed with khaluq, so he did not wipe over my head and did not touch me, and nothing kept him from that except that my mother had perfumed me with khaluq, so he did not touch me because of the khaluq."
"19900","407 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Ali ibn Ma'bad al-Raqqi narrated, Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj, from Abu Musa Abd Allah al-Hamdani, from al-Walid ibn Uqbah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19901","408 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj, from Abd Allah al-Hamdani, from Abu Musa, from al-Walid ibn Uqbah, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) opened Makkah, the people of Makkah began bringing their children to him, and he would wipe over their heads and supplicate for them for blessing, so I was brought to him while I was perfumed with khaluq, so he did not wipe my head, and nothing kept him from that except that my mother had perfumed me with khaluq, so he did not wipe my head because of the khaluq. Abu al-Qasim said: Thus Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated it, from Ja'far, from Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj, from Abd Allah al-Hamdani, from Abu Musa, from al-Walid ibn Uqbah, and what is correct is from Abd Allah al-Hamdani Abu Musa, from al-Walid ibn Uqbah."
"19902","al-Walid ibn Qays 409 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn informed, from Wahb ibn Uqbah, from al-Walid ibn Qays, he said: I had leprosy, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for me and I was healed of it."
"19903","al-Walid ibn al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Makhzum 410 - Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbadah al-Wasiti narrated, Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated, Isma'il ibn Ayyub ibn Salamah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Makhzum narrated: that al-Walid was held in Makkah, so when he wanted to emigrate he sold property of his called al-Mana for a she-camel in al-Taif, and he said: So he found an inattention of the people from him, so he went out he and Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah ibn al-Mughirah, and Salamah ibn Hisham, on foot fearing pursuit, so they hastened until they were worn out, and al-Walid fell short and said: So when he was at Harrat al-Adras he stumbled, so he said: My way, so he entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am exhausted, and I am dying, so shroud me in your shirt and make it what was next to my skin, so he died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shrouded him in his shirt, and he entered upon Umm Salamah while before her was a boy and she was saying: Gadaqa, so he said: You were about to take al-Walid as a paradise, so he named him Abd Allah."
"19904","Those named Waraqah. Waraqah ibn Nawfal al-Dayli, and it is said al-Ansari 411 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Rawh ibn Musafir narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Waraqah al-Ansari, he said: I said: O Muhammad, how does the one who comes to you come to you? Meaning Jibril, peace be upon him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He comes to me from the sky, his two wings pearl, and the soles of his feet green."
"19905","Those named Wabr. Wabr ibn Mushhir al-Hanafi 412 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah, and Abu Ubayd Allah Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Mahdi al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, both said: al-Qadi narrated, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Asbati narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah al-Hizami narrated, Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i narrated to me, Hajib ibn Qudamah al-Hanafi narrated to me, Isa ibn Khuthaym narrated to me, Wabr ibn Mushhir al-Hanafi narrated to me, he said: Musaylimah, and Ibn Shilghaf, and Ibn al-Nawwahah sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so we came to him, and the two went ahead of me in speech, and they were older than me, so they testified, then they said: We testify that you are a prophet and that Musaylimah is after you, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you say, O boy? I said: I testify to what you testified to and I belie what you belied, he said: So I testify to the number of the dust of the world that Musaylimah is a liar, then he said: Seize them both, so they were seized and ordered with them to the house of Kaysan, then a man of his Companions interceded for them, so he released them."
"19906","Those named Waqid. Waqid, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) 413 - Ubayd al-Ijl narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marrudhi narrated, from al-Haytham ibn Jammaz, from al-Harith ibn Hassan, from Zad han, from Waqid, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever obeys Allah, mighty and majestic, has remembered Him, even if his prayer and fasting and recitation of the Qur'an are little, and whoever disobeys Allah has not remembered Him, even if his prayer and fasting and recitation of the Qur'an are much."
"19907","414 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il al-Nahdi narrated, Jumay' ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ijli narrated, he said: A man in Makkah narrated to me, from a son of Abu Halah al-Tamimi, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, he said: I asked my maternal uncle Hind ibn Abi Halah al-Tamimi, and he was descriptive, about the description of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while I desired that he describe to me something of it to hold to, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was magnificent, venerated, his face shining like the shining of the moon on the night of full moon, taller than the medium-statured, shorter than the lanky, great of head, wavy-haired; if his braid parted he parted it, otherwise his hair did not pass the lobes of his ears when he let it grow, bright of color, wide of forehead, thick of eyebrows, long in them without joinedness, between them a vein that anger fills, aquiline of nose, with a light above it, one who reflects upon him thinks him high-nosed, dense of beard, smooth of cheeks, wide of mouth, bright-toothed, split between the teeth, fine of the line of hair, as if his neck is the neck of a statue in the purity of silver, proportionate of build, stout, firm, equal of belly and chest, broad of chest, far between the shoulders, large of joints, bright of bare skin, joined between the throat-pit and navel with hair running like a line, bare of breasts and belly apart from that, hairy of forearms and shoulders and upper chest, long of forearms, wide of palm, smooth of limbs, thick of hands and feet, even of extremities, hollow of soles, smooth of feet so that water runs off them, when he moved he moved with vigor, stepping with humility, walking gently, wide-striding; when he walked it is as if he descends from a slope, and when he turned he turned altogether, lowering the gaze, his look to the earth longer than his look to the sky, most of his look observation, driving his Companions, greeting first whom he met. I said: Describe to me his speech. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was continuous in sorrow, constant in thought, with no rest, not speaking except out of need, long in silence, opening speech and sealing it with his mouth-corners, speaking with comprehensive words, decisive, neither excess nor shortcoming, gentle, neither harsh nor base, magnifying blessing even if small, blaming nothing of it, neither blaming a taste nor praising it, the world and what was of it did not anger him, and when truth was violated no one knew him, and nothing stood before his anger until he avenged it; he did not anger for himself nor avenge for it. When he gestured he gestured with his whole hand, and when he marveled he turned it, and when he spoke he joined with it, striking the inside of his right palm on the inside of his left thumb, and when he angered he turned away and averted, and when he rejoiced he lowered his gaze; most of his laughter was smiling, parting from like hailstones of cloud. He said: So I concealed it from al-Husayn for a time, then I told him, and I found he had preceded me to it, and he had asked him about what I asked him, and I found he had asked his father about his entering and his sitting and his going out and his shape, and left nothing of it. al-Husayn said: I asked my father about the entering of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: His entering was for himself, permitted to him in that; when he retired to his house he divided himself - his entering - into three parts: a part for Allah, a part for his family, and a part for himself, then a part he divided between him and the people, returning that to the common folk through the elite, sparing them nothing. Of his conduct in the portion of the community was preferring the people of merit by his permission, and dividing according to their merit in religion; among them one of need, among them one of two needs, among them one of needs, so he occupies himself with them in what sets them and the community right, by asking about him, and informing them of what befits them, and saying: Let the witness convey to the absent, and convey to me the need of one who cannot convey it to me, for whoever conveys to a ruler the need of one who cannot convey it to him, Allah will make his feet firm on the Day of Resurrection; nothing is mentioned to him except that, and he accepts from no one other than it. They enter as seekers and do not part except from tasting, and go out as guides. He said: So I asked him about his going out, how he acted in it? So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) guarded his tongue except for what concerned them, and brought them together and did not divide them - or he said: repel them - so he honored the noble of every people and put him in charge over them, and warned the people and was cautious of them without folding from anyone his cheerfulness nor his character, inquiring after his Companions and asking the people about what is among the people, beautifying the good and strengthening it, and uglifying the ugly and weakening it, moderate in affair, not differing, not heedless lest they be heedless, and incline; for every state with him is preparation; not falling short of truth nor exceeding it. Those nearest him of the people are their best; the best of them to him is the most general of them in counsel, and the greatest of them to him in rank the best of them in consolation and support. So I asked him about his sitting. So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not sit nor stand except upon remembrance of Allah; he did not settle places and forbade settling them, and when he came to a people he sat where the sitting ended with him and ordered with that, and gave each of his sitters his share; his sitter does not think anyone more honored to him than him. Whoever sat with him or stood with him for a need, he endured with him until he is the one who departs, and whoever asked him a need he did not return him except with it or with an easy word. His spreading and character embraced the people, so he became to them a father, and they became to him in truth equal. His sitting was a sitting of forbearance and modesty and patience and trust; voices are not raised in it, nor sanctities violated in it, nor its slips divulged, equal, excelling in it by piety, humble, honoring the elder, merciful to the young, preferring the needy, guarding the stranger. He said: I said: How was his conduct among his sitters? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was constant in cheerfulness, easy in character, soft of side, neither coarse nor harsh nor clamorous nor foul nor fault-finding nor praising; he overlooks what he dislikes, and none is despaired of him, nor disappointed in him. He left himself from three: argument, excess, and what does not concern him; and he left himself from three: he would blame no one, nor shame him, nor seek his faults, nor speak except in what he hoped its reward. When he spoke his sitters bowed their heads as if birds are upon their heads, and when he fell silent they spoke, and they do not dispute with him. Whoever spoke they listened to him until he finishes; their talk with him is the talk of their first; he laughs at what they laugh at, and marvels at what they marvel at, and endures the stranger for harshness of his speech and question, until his Companions would attract them; and he says: When you see a seeker of need seeking it, then guide him; and he accepts no praise except from one requiting, and does not cut anyone's talk until he exceeds, then cuts it by forbidding or standing. He said: I said: How was the silence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The silence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon four: upon forbearance, caution, estimation, and thought. As for his estimation, then in his leveling look and listening among the people; and as for his remembrance - or he said: his thought - then in what remains and perishes. And forbearance was gathered to him in patience, so nothing made him angry - anger him - nor provoked him. And caution was gathered to him in four: his taking with the good to be followed, his leaving the ugly to be refrained from, his striving of opinion in what sets his community right, and standing in what was gathered for them of the affair of this world and the Hereafter. Abu Ubayd said: Abu Halah was the husband of Khadijah before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his name is al-Nabbash, and his son Hind ibn al-Nabbash is of Banu Usayyid ibn Amr ibn Tamim. Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz said: al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to me, he said: Umar ibn Abi Bakr al-Mawsili narrated to me, he said: Abu Halah is Malik ibn Zurarah of Banu Nabush ibn Zurarah."
"19908","Those named Hulb. Hulb Abu Qabisah al-Ta'i 415 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Sufyan narrated, (H) and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Simak ibn Harb, Qabisah ibn Hulb narrated, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would turn away at times to his right, and at times to his left."
"19909","416 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, (H) and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, (H) and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, they said: Shu'bah narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I saw him turn away from both his sides. This is the wording of Muslim, and Sulayman ibn Harb said: Turning away to his right and to his left."
"19910","417 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and he used to lead us in prayer, then turn away to his right and to his left, from both his sides."
"19911","418 - Muhammad ibn al-Nasr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, Za'idah narrated, from Simak, from Qabisah ibn Hulb al-Ta'i, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would turn when he prayed to his right and to his left, meaning the salutation."
"19912","419 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray with us, then turn away to his right and to his left."
"19913","420 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead us, and he would turn away to both his sides."
"19914","421 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, (H) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would hold with his right upon his left in prayer."
"19915","422 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated, from Simak, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, that he: saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand praying, he said: So I saw him when he placed one of his hands upon the other, the right upon the left."
"19916","423 - Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated, Hafs ibn Jumay' narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would place his hands, one of them upon the other, in prayer."
"19917","424 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead us, then take his left with his right."
"19918","Chapter 425 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, food that I do not leave except out of scruple, so he said: Let nothing stir in your chest resembling in it Christianity."
"19919","426 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated, Sharik narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the food of the Christians, so he said: Let no food stir in your chest resembling in it Christianity. He said: And I saw him placing one of his hands upon the other."
"19920","427 - And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then a man came to him and said: Food that I am scrupulous about, shall I eat it? He said: Let nothing stir in your chest containing Christianity."
"19921","428 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us, my father narrated, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated, Simak ibn Harb narrated, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man asked him and said: Indeed among food is food I am scrupulous about, so he said: Let nothing stir in your chest resembling Christianity."
"19922","429 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated, Husayn ibn Ali narrated, from Za'idah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I leave food for a purpose in myself from it, something, so he said: Let nothing stir in yourself or your chest resembling in it Christianity."
"19923","430 - Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated, Hafs ibn Jumay' narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We leave food out of scruple from it, so he said: Let no food stir in your chest resembling in it Christianity."
"19924","431 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the food of the Christians, so he said: Let no food stir in your chest resembling in it Christianity."
"19925","432 - Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Asbahani narrated to me, Salamah ibn Shabib narrated, Abd Allah ibn al-Wazir al-Ta'ifi narrated, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked: Is there any hour of time that withholds us from prayer? So he said: No, except at the rising of the sun and at its setting, for it rises between the two horns of Satan and sets upon the two horns of Satan."
"19926","Those named Hashim. Hashim ibn Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas, killed with Ali on the day of Siffin 433 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated, from Sinan ibn Harun, Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Ali prayed on the day of Siffin over Ammar ibn Yasir and Hashim ibn Utbah, and Ammar was the nearer of them to Ali, and Hashim was the nearer of them to the qiblah."
"19927","Those named Hisham. Hisham ibn Hakim ibn Hizam ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Qusayy ibn Kilab ibn Murrah ibn Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy ibn Ghalib ibn Fihr ibn Malik, killed at Ajnadayn in the land of Sham 434 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Qatadah al-Sulami, from Hisham ibn Hakim ibn Hizam: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, do we begin deeds or has the decree been decreed? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah took the offspring of Adam from his back, then made them witness over themselves, then poured them forth into a scale, and said: These are in Paradise and these are in the Fire; so the people of Paradise are eased to the deeds of the people of Paradise, and the people of the Fire are eased to the deeds of the people of the Fire."
"19928","435 - al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda' al-Antaki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, al-Zubaydi narrated to me, Rashid ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Qatadah al-Sulami, from his father, from Hisham ibn Hakim: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, do we begin deeds or has the decree been decreed? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah took the offspring of Adam from his back, then made them witness over themselves {Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes}, then poured forth into a scale and said: These are in Paradise and these are in the Fire; as for the people of Paradise, they are eased to the deeds of the people of Paradise, and as for the people of the Fire, they are eased to the deeds of the people of the Fire."
"19929","436 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed, Ma'mar informed, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: Hisham ibn Hakim ibn Hizam entered upon Umayr ibn Sa'd al-Ansari in Sham, and he was a governor for Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he found with him some Nabateans kept in the sun, so he said: What is the matter with these? He said: I held them for the jizyah, so Hisham said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed the one who torments people in this world, Allah will torment him in the Hereafter, so Umayr released them and left them."
"19930","437 - al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Hisham ibn Hakim, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed Allah will torment on the Day of Resurrection those who torment people in this world."
"19931","438 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Hisham ibn Hakim, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19932","439 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Hisham ibn Hakim ibn Hizam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19933","440 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'dah - nephew of al-Zuhri - narrated, from his uncle, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me: that Iyad ibn Ghanm and Hisham ibn Hakim ibn Hizam passed by the governor of Hims while he had kept Nabateans in the sun, so one of them said to the governor: What is this, O so-and-so? Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed Allah torments those who torment people in this world."
"19934","441 - al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to me, Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya narrated to me, al-Zuhri narrated to me, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me: that Hisham ibn Hakim ibn Hizam found Iyad ibn Ghanm while he was over Hims, having kept some Nabateans in the sun for payment of the jizyah, so Hisham ibn Hakim said: What is this, O Iyad? Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed Allah torments those who torment people in this world."
"19935","Hisham ibn Amir al-Ansari. al-Hasan from Hisham 442 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Hisham ibn Amir, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: What is your name? So he said: Shihab. He said: Rather you are Hisham."
"19936","Humayd ibn Hilal from Hisham ibn Amir 443 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated, from Humayd ibn Hilal, he said: Hisham ibn Amir came to prayer and hastened walking and entered prayer, while breath had hurried him, so he recited aloud behind the imam; so when he finished his prayer it was said to him: Do you recite behind the imam? He said: We do so."
"19937","444 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed, Ma'mar and Ibn Uyaynah informed, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, he said: Hisham ibn Amir informed me, he said: My father was killed on the day of Uhud, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dig and widen and do well, and bury two and three in one grave, and put forward the most Qur'an of them. And my father was third of three, and he was the most Qur'an of them, so he was put forward."
"19938","445 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hisham ibn Amir, he said: Wounds were severe on the day of Uhud, so they complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the wounds, so he said: Dig and widen and do well, and bury two and three in the grave, and put forward the most Qur'an of them. So they put my father forward before two men."
"19939","446 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hisham ibn Amir, the like of it."
"19940","447 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated, from Sufyan, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hisham ibn Amir, he said: They complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of wounds and of digging for each person on the day of Uhud, so he said: Dig and deepen and do well, and bury two and three in a grave. They said: Whom shall we put forward? He said: The most Qur'an of them."
"19941","448 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abd al-Warith narrated, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu al-Dahma, from Hisham ibn Amir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dig and do well and widen, and bury two and three in a grave, and put forward the most Qur'an of them. So my father was put forward before two men. Abd al-Warith added in the chain of this hadith Abu al-Dahma."
"19942","449 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, (H) and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, (H) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated, from Humayd ibn Hilal, he said: Hisham ibn Amir said: The Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud and said: O Messenger of Allah, wounds and hardship, so what do you command us? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dig and widen, and put two men and three in the grave. So they said: Which of them shall we put forward? He said: Put forward the most Qur'an of them. So they put my father forward between two men or two."
"19943","450 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to me, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hisham ibn Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no trial between the creation of Adam until the Hour comes greater than the Dajjal."
"19944","451 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal: that Hisham ibn Amir said: You pass over me to a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they were not more attached to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than me, nor more memorizing than me. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no trial between the creation of Adam and the standing of the Hour greater than the Dajjal."
"19945","452 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Qatadah, from Hisham ibn Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no matter between the creation of Adam until the standing of the Hour greater than the Dajjal."
"19946","453 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated, from Humayd ibn Hilal, he said: Hisham ibn Amir saw men passing over him to Imran ibn Husayn and to others of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: You pass on to men who were not more present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than me, nor more eager for his hadith than me, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no trial between the creation of Adam until the Hour comes greater than the trial of the Dajjal."
"19947","Mu'adhah al-Adawiyyah from Hisham ibn Amir 454 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Hakkam narrated, Shu'bah ibn Yazid al-Rishk narrated, from Mu'adhah, from Hisham ibn Amir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon a Muslim for more than three nights, for they are both deviating from truth so long as they persist in cutting off; and the first of them to return, his preceding in returning is its expiation. And if he greets him and he does not accept, and does not return his greeting, the angels return it upon him, and Satan returns upon the other. And if they die upon their cutting off, they will not enter Paradise."
"19948","455 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated, Abd al-Warith narrated, Yazid al-Rishk narrated, Mu'adhah narrated to me that she heard Hisham ibn Amir al-Ansari saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful for a Muslim to cut off a Muslim for more than three; they, so long as they cut off, are deviating from truth. And the first of them to return, his preceding in returning is an expiation; and because if they die in their cutting off they will not enter Paradise together ever. And if he greets him and he does not accept his greeting and his peace, the angel returns upon him, and upon the other Satan."
"19949","Abu Qilabah from Hisham ibn Amir 456 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed, Ma'mar informed, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Hisham ibn Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the head of the Dajjal from behind it is matted, and he will say: I am your lord; so whoever says: You are my lord, is trialed, and whoever says: You lie, my Lord is Allah, upon Him I rely and to Him I turn, it will not harm him - or he said: Then there is no trial upon him."
"19950","457 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated, (H) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf the judge narrated to us, both said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, he said: Hisham ibn Amir came to Basrah and found them trading gold in their stipends, so he stood and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling gold for silver on credit, and informed us that that is usury. And the wording is of Sulayman ibn Harb."
"19951","458 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Ayyub, he said: I heard Abu Qilabah, while the people in the time of Ibn Ziyad were taking dinars for dirhams on credit, so a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Hisham ibn Amir stood and said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling gold for silver on credit, and informed us that that is of usury."
"19952","459 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Shabbabah narrated, Sa'id ibn Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated, from Abu Qilabah, he said: There were people in Basrah in the time of Ziyad taking dirhams for dinars on credit, so a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Hisham ibn Amir al-Ansari stood and said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling gold for silver on credit, and informed us that that is usury."
"19953","Abu Qatadah from Hisham ibn Amir 460 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated, Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami narrated, Yahya ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Qatadah al-Adawi, from Hisham ibn Amir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever accuses a believer of disbelief is like killing him."
"19954","Hisham ibn al-As ibn Wa'il al-Sahmi 461 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sons of al-As are believers: Hisham and Amr."
"19955","462 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashir narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: We used to say: There is no repentance for one trialed when he leaves his religion after his Islam and knowledge, so Allah sent down about them {O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah} to His saying {the punishment comes to you suddenly while you do not perceive}. So I wrote it with my hand, then sent with it to Hisham ibn al-As ibn Wa'il. Hisham said: When it came to me I climbed with it thus crying out with it, and saying, and I did not understand it, so it fell in myself that it was sent down about us, and what we used to say. So I sat upon my camel, then joined Madinah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained awaiting to be permitted for emigration, and for his Companions of the emigrants who had come in groups. And Abu Bakr remained with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awaiting to be permitted to set out for him. And Abu Bakr had sought permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in emigration, so he said: Do not hasten; perhaps Allah will make for you a companion. So Abu Bakr hoped that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) meant himself. And Abu Bakr had prepared for that two mounts, feeding them in his house."
"19956","Those named Hani. Hani ibn Yazid Abu Shurayh al-Harithi 463 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini Fustuqah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Yusuf al-Qulusi saying: Abu Shurayh Hani ibn Yazid ibn Nahik ibn Durayd ibn Sufyan ibn Dibab of Banu al-Harith ibn Ka'b. What Hani ibn Yazid transmitted."
"19957","464 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Ali narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father Shurayh, from his grandfather Hani ibn Yazid, that he came as a delegation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among people of his folk, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard him nicknamed Abu al-Hakam, so he said: Why do these nickname you Abu al-Hakam? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I judge between my folk in a matter that is between them, so these and these are pleased, so I was nicknamed Abu al-Hakam, and I have no child, yet I am Abu al-Hakam. He said: Do you have a child? He said: Yes. He said: What is the name of the eldest of them? He said: Shurayh. He said: So you are Abu Shurayh."
"19958","465 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Sharik narrated, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from his grandfather Hani ibn Yazid, he said: I came as a delegation to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he saw them nicknaming me Abu al-Hakam, so he said: Indeed Allah is al-Hakam; why are you nicknamed Abu al-Hakam? I said: When there is something between my folk they refer to me for judgment, so I judge between them and they are pleased with my judgment. He said: And what child have you? I said: Yes. He said: So what is the name of the eldest of them? I said: Shurayh. He said: So you are Abu Shurayh."
"19959","466 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated, Yazid ibn al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh narrated, from his father, from his grandfather Hani ibn Yazid, that he came as a delegation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among his folk, and he heard them while they nickname Hani Abu al-Hakam, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: Indeed Allah is al-Hakam, so why are you nicknamed Abu al-Hakam? With a child? He said: No, but my folk when they differ in something come to me, so I judge between them and each of the two parties is pleased. He said: How good is this."
"19960","467 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from his grandfather Hani, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of something that makes Paradise obligatory for me. He said: What makes Paradise obligatory is feeding food and spreading peace."
"19961","468 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, command me with a deed. He said: Feed food and spread peace."
"19962","469 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: Ibn al-Ashja'i gave me books from his father, and in them was from Sufyan, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed that admits me to Paradise. He said: Indeed among what necessitates forgiveness is offering peace and good speech."
"19963","470 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated, Yazid ibn al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, from his father Hani ibn Yazid, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of something that makes Paradise obligatory. He said: Upon you is good speech and offering food."
"19964","Hani ibn Amr Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, then al-Ka'bi, and it is said: Ka'b ibn Amr, and it is said: Khuwaylid ibn Amr, and he used to reside in Madinah and in it he died. And of his reports 471 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to me, he said: Abu Shurayh al-Ka'bi died, and his name is Khuwaylid, in the year sixty-eight in Madinah, and there was disagreement about his death."
"19965","472 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, he said: Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i Ka'b ibn Amr died in the year fifty-eight."
"19966","473 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini Fustuqah narrated to us, Harun ibn Abd Allah al-Hammal narrated, he said: Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i is Ka'b ibn Amr, and it is said: Khuwaylid ibn Amr, and it is said: Amr ibn Khuwaylid."
"19967","474 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated, Abu Ma'shar narrated, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, he said: Abu Shurayh al-Ka'bi said: Whoever sees me disputing with an in-law of mine, I spreading for him my noblewoman and he spreading for me his noblewoman, then I am at that time mad, so brand my head; and whoever sees for Abu Shurayh a young goat or milk sold in the market, then it is my plunder; and whoever sees me disputing with a neighbor of mine over a brick, then I am mad, so brand my head. So a neighbor of his called Ajrafah tested him and took ten cubits from his house, so they said to him: O Abu Shurayh, he has taken ten cubits from your house, so he said: He knows best. He said: So his neighbor returned it to him after, and returned to his right."
"19968","What Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i transmitted. Sa'id al-Maqburi from Abu Shurayh 475 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated, from Malik, (H) and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated, Malik informed, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Shurayh al-Ka'bi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or be silent; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. His reward is his day and night, and hospitality is three days; so what is after that is charity. And it is not lawful for him to stay with him until he expels him. And their wording is one."
"19969","476 - al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, (H) and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, both said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to me, from Abu Shurayh al-Adawi, he said: My two ears heard, and my two eyes saw, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke, so he said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. His reward, they said: And what is his reward, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A day and a night, and hospitality is three; and what is beyond that is charity upon him. And let him not stay with him until he expels him. And he said: And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or be silent."
"19970","477 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated, Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or be silent; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. His reward, it was said: And what is his reward? He said: His day and his night."
"19971","478 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, both said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. His reward is a day and a night, and it is not lawful for him to stay with his host until he expels him. Hospitality is three; so what is spent after upon him is charity."
"19972","479 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sa'id, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hospitality is three days; so what exceeds that is charity."
"19973","Abu Sa'id is Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi. 480 - Ahmad ibn Bishr ibn Habib al-Bayruti narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bakkar narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sa'id, from Abu Shurayh, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or be silent."
"19974","481 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated, Shayban narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Sa'd informed me: that Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or be silent."
"19975","482 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Aban ibn Yazid narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sa'd, he narrated to him, from Abu Shurayh: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or be silent."
"19976","483 - al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Janadi narrated to us, Ali ibn Ziyad al-Lahji narrated, Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq narrated, he said: Ibn Jurayj mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Shurayh, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or be silent."
"19977","484 - al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, (H) and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, both said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to me, from Abu Shurayh al-Adawi: that he said to Amr ibn Sa'id while he was sending expeditions to Makkah: Permit me, O commander, to narrate to you a saying with which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood the morrow of the day of the Conquest; my two ears heard it, and my heart retained it, and my two eyes saw him when he spoke it. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Indeed Makkah, Allah made it sacred, and people did not make it sacred. And it is not lawful for a person believing in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood in it, nor to cut its tree. So if anyone permits fighting by the fighting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then say to him: Indeed Allah permitted to His Messenger and did not permit to you. And He permitted to me in it only an hour of daytime, and its sanctity has returned today as its sanctity yesterday. So let the witness convey to the absent. So it was said to Abu Shurayh: What did Amr say to you? He said: He said: I know of this better than you, O Abu Shurayh; indeed the sanctuary does not shelter a disobedient, nor a fugitive with blood, nor a fugitive with ruin."
"19978","485 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated, (H) and Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, both, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, he said: When Amr ibn Sa'id ibn al-As sent his expedition to Makkah, invading Ibn al-Zubayr, Abu Shurayh came to him and spoke to him and informed him of what he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he went out to the gathering of his folk and sat in it, so I stood to him and sat with him, and he narrated to his folk as he narrated to Amr ibn Sa'id. Abu Shurayh said: So I said: O this, we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he opened Makkah, so when it was the morrow of the day of the Conquest, Khuza'ah fell upon a man of Hudhayl and killed him while he was a polytheist. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood as a speaker and said: O people, indeed Allah made Makkah sacred the day He created the heavens and the earth, so it is sacred by the sacredness of Allah until the Day of Resurrection. It is not lawful for a person believing in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood in it, nor to cut a tree in it. It was not made lawful for anyone before me, nor will it be made lawful for anyone after me, and it was not made lawful to me except this hour, in anger over its people. Lo, then its sanctity returned as its sanctity yesterday. So let the witness of you convey to the absent. So whoever says to you: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fought in it, then say: Indeed Allah made it lawful for His Messenger and did not make it lawful for you. O company of Khuza'ah, lift your hands from killing, for it has grown grave to occur. You have killed a slain one, I shall surely pay his blood-money. So whoever kills after this station of mine, then his family are with the better of two views: if they wish they ransom by his killer, and if they wish by his blood-money. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid the blood-money of the man who was killed of Hudhayl. And the wording is of the hadith of al-Nufayli."
"19979","486 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Shurayh, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah made Makkah sacred, and people did not make it sacred. So it is not lawful for one who believes in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood in it, nor to cut a tree in it. So if anyone permits by it, and says: It was made lawful for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then indeed Allah made it lawful for me an hour of daytime, and did not make it lawful for anyone other than me. Then it is sacred as its sanctity yesterday. O Khuza'ah: you killed this slain one of Hudhayl, and I by Allah shall pay his blood-money. So whoever kills in it a slain one after this, then his family are between two choices: if they love they kill, and if they love they take the blood-money."
"19980","487 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated, (H) and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, (H) and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, they said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Shurayh al-Ka'bi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah he does not believe, by Allah he does not believe, by Allah he does not believe. They said: And who is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The neighbor whose neighbor is not safe from his harms. They said: And what are his harms? He said: His evil. And the wording is of the hadith of Asim ibn Ali."
"19981","488 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Salamah ibn Abi Kabshah narrated, Safwan ibn Isa narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Shurayh ibn Amr al-Khuza'i, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of sitting upon the roads; so whoever of you sits on the road, let him give it its right. We said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is its right? He said: Lowering the gaze, returning the greeting, commanding the good, and forbidding the evil."
"19982","489 - Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Sa'd ibn Sa'id narrated, from his brother, from his father, from Abu Shurayh, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19983","490 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from al-Ala ibn Kathir, from Dawud ibn Ayyub al-Madini, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Shurayh: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a shield; so if he completes, then for you; and if he falls short, then upon him the shortcoming, and for you the completion."
"19984","491 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated, (H) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Asbahani narrated, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar informed, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: Rejoice; do you not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? They said: Yes. He said: Indeed this Qur'an is a rope, its end in the Hand of Allah, and its end in your hands; so hold to it, for you will never go astray nor perish after it ever."
"19985","492 - al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus Abu Muslim al-Mustamli narrated, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated, Ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Shurayh al-Ka'bi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What does a neighbor hope from his neighbor when he does not raise for him a beam upon his wall."
"19986","493 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated, al-Walid ibn Ata ibn al-Agharr narrated, Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman brother of Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated, Abu Hazim narrated, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes a span of land unjustly, it will be hung upon him on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."
"19987","Sufyan ibn Abi al-Awja from Abu Shurayh 494 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Harith ibn Fudayl, from Sufyan ibn Abi al-Awja, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is afflicted by killing or wounding, then he chooses one of three: either to take in retaliation, or to pardon, or to take the blood-money; so if he takes the blood-money, then seize upon his hand, for if he transgresses after that, then for him is the Fire of Hell."
"19988","495 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Harith ibn Fudayl, from Ibn Abi al-Awja, from Abu Shurayh, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is afflicted by blood or wounding - and wounding is the wound - then he is with choice between one of three; so if he wants the fourth, then seize upon his hand: to kill, to pardon, or to take the blood-money. So whoever does something of that then returns in it, then for him is the Fire of Hell, abiding eternally therein forever."
"19989","496 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq, al-Harith ibn Fudayl narrated to me, from Sufyan ibn Abi al-Awja, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is afflicted by blood or wounding, then its owner is with choice between one of three: either to take in retaliation, or to pardon, or to take the blood-money; so if he wants the fourth, then seize upon his hand. So if he chooses something of that then goes beyond to the fourth, then he is in the Fire, abiding eternally therein."
"19990","497 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed, from al-Harith ibn Fudayl, from Sufyan ibn Abi al-Awja, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is afflicted by blood or wounding, then he is between one of three; so if he wants the fourth, then seize upon his hand: between to take in retaliation, or to pardon, or to take the blood-money. So if he takes one then transgresses after that, then for him is the Fire, abiding eternally therein forever."
"19991","Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi from Abu Shurayh 498 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Shurayh, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the most insolent of people against Allah is a man who kills other than his killer, or seeks by the blood of Jahiliyyah from the people of Islam; and whoever makes his eyes see in sleep what they did not see."
"19992","499 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Shurayh, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19993","Muslim ibn Yazid al-Sa'di from Abu Shurayh 500 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that Muslim ibn Yazid, one of Banu Sa'd, narrated to him that Abu Shurayh ibn Amr al-Khuza'i informed him, and he was of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that Banu Ka'b on the day of the Conquest met a man of Hudhayl whom they sought for a blood-debt in Jahiliyyah in the sanctuary, heading to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge to him upon Islam, and they killed him. So when the killing reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he angered the severest anger he angered. So Banu Ka'b hastened to Abu Bakr and Umar and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), seeking their intercession to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So when it was evening he stood among the people and praised Allah with what He is worthy of, then said: As for after, indeed Allah made Makkah sacred and people did not make it sacred; and Allah made it lawful to me only an hour of daytime yesterday, then it is sacred as Allah made it sacred. And the most hostile of people against Allah are three: a man who kills in it, and a man who kills other than his killer for the blood-debt of Jahiliyyah, and by Allah I shall surely pay the blood-money of this man whom you struck. Abu Shurayh said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid his blood-money."
"19994","Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from Abu Shurayh 501 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, (H) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, they said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, he heard Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im informing, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him do good to his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or be silent."
"19995","Hani ibn Niyar ibn Amr ibn Ubayd ibn Kilab ibn Duhman ibn Ghanm ibn Dhibyan ibn Kahil ibn Dihl ibn Bali ibn Amr ibn al-Haf ibn Quda'ah Abu Burdah al-Balawi, ally of Banu Harithah ibn al-Khazraj, Aqabi, Badri, and he is the maternal uncle of al-Bara ibn Azib. 502 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah: In the naming of who witnessed al-Aqabah of the Ansar, then of Banu Harithah: Abu Burdah ibn Niyar ibn Amr ibn Ubayd, and he is an ally to them of Bali, and he is Badri."
"19996","503 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: In the naming of who witnessed al-Aqabah of the Ansar, then of Banu Harithah: Abu Burdah ibn Niyar ibn Amr."
"19997","What Abu Burdah ibn Niyar transmitted 504 - Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Atiyyah ibn Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid said: My father narrated to me, Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to me, Busr ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to me, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: My maternal uncle, brother of my mother, narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the first of the rites of this day - for the day of sacrifice - prayer, then sacrifice after prayer. So I walked to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered before I prayed, and with me is a young she-goat, offspring of a jadha'ah, dearer to me than the meat of two sheep; shall I slaughter it? He said: Yes, and it will not suffice for anyone after you."
"19998","505 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sari' al-Kufi narrated, Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, from his maternal uncle Abu Burdah, he said: I took the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of sacrifice and went with him to the house, so I said to the slave-girl: Feed us of the meat of your sacrifice. So he said: It is not a sacrifice; it is only a sheep of meat. The sacrifice is only after prayer. I said: O Messenger of Allah, with us is a young she-goat of ours, a jadha'ah; shall I sacrifice with it? He said: Yes, and it will not suffice for anyone after you."
"19999","506 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, from Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, he said: I slaughtered a sheep, then mentioned the hadith the like of it."
"20000","507 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, from his maternal uncle Abu Burdah ibn Niyar: that he hastened a sheep, then mentioned it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O Messenger of Allah, I hastened the sheep of the young for us? So he said: Before prayer? He said: Yes. So he said: That is a sheep of meat. He said: Then with me is a jadha'ah dearer to me than a musinnah; will it suffice for me? He said: Yes, and it will never suffice for anyone after you."
"20001","508 - al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Umar ibn al-Sa'ib, from Bushayr ibn Yasar: that Abu Burdah ibn Niyar sacrificed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed. He said: Then I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I went out with my sacrifice to the prayer-place and slaughtered it before prayer. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sacrifice another. So I sought of goats and did not find, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to sacrifice a jadha' of sheep."
"20002","509 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il narrated, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated, from al-Suddi, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara, he said: I met my maternal uncle, and with him was a banner, so I said: Where are you going? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a man who married the wife of his father after him, to strike his neck and kill him."
"20003","510 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Mubarak al-Kufi narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara, he said: My maternal uncle Abu Burdah passed by me, and with him was a banner, so I said: To where? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a man who married the wife of his father, to bring him his head."
"20004","511 - Muhammad ibn Fada al-Jawhari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Abu Burdah ibn Niyar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the tribes supplicating for them, and left a tribe he did not come to, so they disapproved that. So they searched the goods of a companion of theirs and found a necklace in the saddle-cloth of a man of them which he had misappropriated, so they returned it; then he came to them and prayed over them."
"20005","512 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, al-Walid ibn Abd Allah ibn Jumay' narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm narrated to me, he said: Abu Burdah narrated to me, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The world will not pass until it is with a Luka' son of Luka'."
"20006","513 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abu Usamah narrated, from Sa'id ibn Umayr ibn Uqbah ibn Niyar al-Ansari, from his uncle Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant of my community prays upon me a prayer, truthful in it in his heart, except that Allah prays upon him with it ten prayers, and writes for him with it ten good deeds, and raises for him with it ten degrees, and erases from him with it ten evil deeds."
"20007","514 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful for anyone to strike anyone more than ten lashes, except in a hadd of the hudud of Allah."
"20008","515 - al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Salih Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: None is flogged more than ten lashes except in a hadd of the hudud of Allah."
"20009","516 - Abu Urubah al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu al-Mu'afa narrated, Muhammad ibn Maslamah narrated, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir, from Abu Burdah ibn Niyar al-Ansari, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No flogging more than ten lashes except in a hadd of the hudud of Allah."
"20010","517 - Abu al-Jarud Mas'ud ibn Muhammad al-Ramli narrated to us, Imran al-Sufi narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, Bukayr ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir, Abu Burdah ibn Niyar narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None is flogged ten lashes except in a hadd of the hudud of Allah."
"20011","518 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-'Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi' ibn Yazid narrated to us, Abu Sakhr narrated to me, from 'Abd Allah ibn Mughith or Mughith - Ibn Abi Maryam doubted -, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There will come forth from al-Kahinayn a man who will study the Qur'an with a study that no one after him will study."""
"20012","519 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Isa, from Jumay' ibn 'Umayr, or 'Umayr ibn Jumay', from his maternal uncle Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, and he was a Companion, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which earning is best? He said: ""The work of a man with his hand."""
"20013","520 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Wa'il ibn Dawud, from Jumay' ibn 'Umayr, from his maternal uncle Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best earning of a man is his child, and every blessed sale."""
"20014","521 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Isa, from Jumay' ibn 'Umayr, from Abu Burdah, he said: I was walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of the roads of Madinah, and he passed by food and put his hand in and brought out poor-quality food on his hand, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He who cheats is not of us."""
"20015","522 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us; (ha) and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim Salam al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn 'Uthman narrated to us; (ha) and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us; (ha) and 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Qasim ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Drink from vessels but do not become intoxicated."""
"20016","Hani Abu Malik. 523 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Abi Malik narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Hani Abu Malik: that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Yemen, and he invited him to Islam and he accepted Islam, and he wiped over his head and supplicated for him for blessing, and lodged him with Yazid ibn Abi Sufyan. Then when Abu Bakr equipped the army to Sham, he went out with them and did not return."
"20017","Those named Hilal. Hilal ibn al-Harith Abu al-Hamra, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who used to reside in Hims. 524 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Abu al-Hamra, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pass by a man who had food in a container, and he looked at it and said: ""Have you cheated? Whoever cheats us is not of us."""
"20018","525 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: I heard Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad say: I heard Abu Dawud say: I heard Abu al-Hamra say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come to the door of 'Ali and Fatimah for six months, saying: {Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly}."
"20019","526 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abadah ibn Ziyad al-Asadi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah al-Thumali, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Abu al-Hamra, the servant of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When I was taken up to the heaven, I entered Paradise and saw written on the leg of the Throne: There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I aided him with 'Ali and helped him."""
"20020","Those named Habbar. Habbar ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib ibn Asad ibn 'Abd al-'Uzza ibn Qusayy. 527 - Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani, with his lineage, narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"20021","What Habbar ibn al-Aswad transmitted. 528 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya al-'Abdasi narrated to us, Hushaym ibn Abi Ma'shar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn Habbar ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by the house of Habbar ibn al-Aswad and heard the sound of singing, and said: ""What is this?"" It was said: A wedding. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying: ""This is marriage, not fornication,"" repeating it."
"20022","529 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hawbar ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah, from 'Abd Allah ibn Habbar, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: Habbar married off his daughter, and at her wedding drums and sieves were beaten, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard that and said: ""What is this?"" They said: Habbar has married off his daughter, and drums and sieves were beaten at her wedding. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Announce the marriage, announce the marriage; this is marriage, not fornication."""
"20023","Those named Hazzal. Hazzal. 530 - Abu Yazid Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Yazid ibn Nu'aym ibn Hazzal, from his grandfather, that he said to Ma'iz ibn Malik: Go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and inform him of your story. So he came to him and informed him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him repeatedly. He kept repeating that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to his people and said: ""Is he mad?"" They said: No. He said: ""A virgin or previously married?"" They said: Rather previously married. He said: Then he ordered him to be stoned. He said: Woe to you, O Hazzal, had you covered him with your cloak it would have been better for you."
"20024","531 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Nu'aym ibn Hazzal narrated to me, from his grandfather Hazzal, he said: There was a slave girl grazing sheep for her family, and a man of ours called Ma'iz ibn Malik came to her and had intercourse with her. She came and informed my grandfather Hazzal, so my grandfather Hazzal kept urging him to confess before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Woe to you, if you do not do so Allah will send down upon His Messenger and inform him of your story. He kept on until Ma'iz ibn Malik came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, he has committed adultery. He turned away from him three or four times, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to be stoned. He said: A man confronted him with a camel's jawbone and struck his leg with it and knocked him down, and they stoned him until they killed him, while he was crying out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""As for he, had he come to me he would not have been rejected for that."" Then he said to the one who had urged him: Woe to you, O Hazzal, had you covered him with your garment it would have been better for you, and he struck with his hand upon the knee of Hazzal."
"20025","Those named Hirmas. Hirmas ibn Ziyad al-Bahili. 532 - Muhammad ibn Habban al-Mazini narrated to us, Yusuf ibn 'Anbas al-Yamami narrated to us, 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar al-Yamami narrated to us, he said: I went out for Hajj and came to al-Muqtarab - the Muqtarab of Bahilah - and met al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad, and he informed me, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina on a she-camel, with al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas riding behind him."
"20026","533 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad narrated to me, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was riding behind my father, and he was on his she-camel al-'Adba on the Day of Sacrifice with the people around him. I said to my father: What is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying? He said: He says: ""Stone the Jamarat with pebbles like chickpea-sized stones."""
"20027","534 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn 'Imran al-Razi narrated to us; (ha) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Durays narrated to us, 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, from al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad, he said: I was riding behind my father and saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a camel saying: ""Here I am for Hajj and 'Umrah together."""
"20028","535 - Al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Fayid narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar, from al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The beggar has a right even if he comes on a horse."""
"20029","536 - 'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Yunus ibn Jamil narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Fayid al-Qurashi narrated to us, 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, from Hirmas ibn Ziyad, he said: A man of my people gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dates as a gift, and he said: ""What dates are these?"" He said: Al-Judhami. He said: ""O Allah, bless al-Judhami."""
"20030","537 - Abu 'Arubah al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Umayyah 'Amr ibn Hisham al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Qatadah al-Harrani narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar, from al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying on his mount toward the east."""
"20031","538 - Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Naysaburi narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mulayhah narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar, from al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching on his she-camel, saying: ""Beware of treachery, for it is an evil inner lining, and beware of injustice, for it is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection, and beware of miserliness, for it destroyed those before you with miserliness, so they shed their blood and severed their kinship ties."""
"20032","539 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Abu al-Jahm 'Abd al-Ghaffar ibn 'Umar narrated to us, 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, from al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in his sandals."
"20033","540 - Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Abbar, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, and Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: 'Uthman ibn Talut ibn 'Abbad narrated to us, 'Abd al-Salam ibn Hashim al-Bazzar narrated to us, Hanbal ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in his sandals."
"20034","541 - Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-A'raj narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Harb al-Laythi narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Nabil narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching on a red she-camel."
"20035","542 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Abu Tamim al-Jayshani, he said: The gathering brought us together in Atrublus, with us were Hubayb al-Ghifari and 'Amr ibn al-'As, Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 'Amr said: ""The best of Ramadan,"" and al-Ghifari said: ""We do not distinguish between the makeup of Ramadan;"" Allah only said: {A number of other days}."
"20036","What Hubayb transmitted. 543 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Aslam Abu 'Imran, from Hubayb ibn Mughaffal al-Ghifari, that he saw Muhammad ibn 'Ulayyah al-Qurashi stand up from his cloak, and Hubayb looked at him and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever treads it arrogantly will tread it in the Fire."""
"20037","544 - Isma'il ibn Qirat al-Dimashqi and Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us; (ha) and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, they said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Qurrah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Aslam Abu 'Imran informed him, from Hubayb ibn Mughaffal, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever treads it arrogantly will tread it in the Fire"" - meaning his lower garment."
"20038","Those named Hind. Hind ibn Asma al-Bajali. 545 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Habib ibn Hind ibn Asma, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to my people of Aslam and said: ""Command your people to fast this day, the day of 'Ashura; whoever of them you find has eaten at the start of his day should fast the rest of it."""
"20039","The chapter of lam-alif. Lashumah ibn Jurthum Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, and there is disagreement over his name; it is said: Lash ibn Himyar, and it is said: Las ibn 'Asim, and it is said: Jurhum ibn Lashim, and it is said: Jurhum, and it is said: 'Irnuq ibn Nasim, and it is said: Nasir, and it is said: Nashib ibn 'Amr, and it is said: Harim ibn Nashib. 546 - Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Madini Fustuqah narrated to us, Abu Musa Harun ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: ""Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani died in the year seventy-five."""
"20040","What Abu Tha'labah transmitted. 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As from Abu Tha'labah. 547 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Tha'labah, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, give me a ruling concerning lost property. He said: ""Whatever you find on a frequented or inhabited road, announce it for a year; if you do not find its owner it is yours. And whatever you find in an uninhabited village or an unfrequented road, in it is the fifth."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, give me a ruling concerning my bow. He said: ""Eat whatever your bow returns to you."" I said: Even if it disappears from me? He said: ""Even if it disappears from you after you see no trace of an arrow or arrowhead in it."""
"20041","Abu Idris al-Khawlani from Abu Tha'labah. 548 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20042","549 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik; (ha) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20043","550 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, from Abu Tha'labah: ""that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."""
"20044","551 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, from Abu Tha'labah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade snatching, plundering, animals killed by tying, and every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20045","552 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Tha'labah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20046","553 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Yusuf al-Majishun narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from 'A'idh Allah Abu Idris, from Abu Tha'labah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20047","554 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim Abu 'Amir al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Tamim, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, from Abu Tha'labah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declare unlawful the meat of the domestic donkey and every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20048","555 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, from Abu Tha'labah, he said: Every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey was declared unlawful."""
"20049","556 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my uncle narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan: that Abu Idris 'A'idh Allah ibn 'Abd Allah informed him that Abu Tha'labah informed him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20050","557 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me; (ha) and Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us; (ha) and 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20051","558 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, that Abu Idris informed him: that Abu Tha'labah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared unlawful the meat of domestic donkeys."
"20052","559 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey and the meat of domestic donkeys."
"20053","560 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to me, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of domestic donkeys, and that pregnant captives be approached, and every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20054","561 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed me, from the hadith of Abu Idris: that Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20055","562 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Numayr al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Uqayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from 'Uqayl, and Rishdin, from 'Uqayl, and Qurrah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Idris, from Abu Tha'labah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he: forbade the meat of domestic donkeys, and every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20056","563 - 'Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Uzayz narrated to us, Salamah ibn Rawh narrated to us, from 'Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani: that he heard Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20057","564 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, 'Uqayl narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, Abu Idris narrated to me, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared unlawful the meat of domestic donkeys, and the meat of every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20058","565 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from 'A'idh Allah ibn Abi Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared unlawful the meat of every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20059","566 - Al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Janadi narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Ziyad al-Lahji narrated to us, Musa ibn Tariq Abu Qurrah narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah ibn Salih mentioned, from Ya'qub ibn 'Ata, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris: that Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20060","567 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me, Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn 'Amr informed us, from Busr ibn 'Ubayd Allah, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Tha'labah, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the vessels of the polytheists, and he said: ""Eat in them and drink and cook if you find no alternative."" He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20061","568 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Makhul, from Abu Idris, from Abu Tha'labah, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in enemy land and need their vessels. He said: ""Do without them as much as you can; if you find nothing else, wash them and eat and drink in them."""
"20062","569 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd informed me, from Makhul, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade in the year of Khaybar the meat of domestic donkeys, and that a pregnant captive be approached until she gives birth, and every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."
"20063","570 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi; (ha) and 'Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-'Ala ibn Zibriq narrated to us, my father narrated to us; (ha) and 'Umarah ibn Wathimah al-Misri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, Yunus ibn Sayf narrated to us: that Abu Idris 'A'idh Allah narrated to them that Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani narrated to them, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he raised his gaze at him and lowered it, then said: ""Nuwaybah."" Abu Tha'labah said: A Nuwaybah of good or a Nuwaybah of evil? He said: ""A Nuwaybah of good."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land with game; what of it is lawful for us and what is unlawful? He said: ""The domestic donkey and every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey are unlawful, and whatever your bow and your trained dog return to you is lawful for you."" Then he asked him about something concerning the People of the Book and their vessels, and he said: ""If you find sufficiency without them, do not approach them; and if you need them, wash them then eat and drink in them."""
"20064","571 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, he said: I heard Rabi'ah ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi say: I heard Abu Idris al-Khawlani narrate that he heard Abu Tha'labah say: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in the land of the People of the Book; we eat with them in their vessels, and our land is a land of hunting with the bow and the trained dog, and the dog that is not trained. Inform me what is lawful for me of that and what is unlawful? He said: ""As for what you mentioned, that you are in the land of the People of the Book and eat in their vessels: if you find other than their vessels, do not eat in them; and if you find nothing else, wash them and eat in them. And as for what you mentioned of hunting: whatever you hunt with your bow and mention the name of Allah over, eat; and whatever your untrained dog hunts, whatever of it you catch alive eat, and whatever you do not catch alive do not eat of it; and whatever your trained dog hunts, eat of what it holds for you and mention the name of Allah over it."""
"20065","Jubayr ibn Nufayr from Abu Tha'labah. 572 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Abu Tha'labah, Mu'awiyah raised it once and did not raise it another time: Allah will not fail this ummah of half a day; and when you see Sham as the table of a man and his household, then Constantinople will be conquered."
"20066","573 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The jinn are of three kinds: a kind that have wings and fly in the air, a kind that are snakes, and a kind that settle and travel."""
"20067","574 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, 'Uqayl ibn Mudrik narrated to us, from Luqman ibn 'Amir, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr al-Hadrami, that Abu Tha'labah narrated to them that he raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Khaybar, and hunger struck them, and they found domestic donkeys there, and the people slaughtered some of them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told, so he ordered 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf to call out among the people: The meat of domestic donkeys is not lawful for whoever testifies that I am the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they overturned their pots with what was in them, and they found onions and garlic in their gardens and ate of them while hungry, and suffered. When the people went to the mosque, the smell of the mosque was of onion and garlic, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats of this foul tree should not approach us."""
"20068","575 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, Ma'n ibn 'Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Abu Tha'labah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning one who finds his game after three days: ""He may eat unless it has rotted."""
"20069","576 - Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Abu Tha'labah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""My Lord will not fail to delay my ummah half a day."""
"20070","577 - Musa ibn 'Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, my father narrated to us; (ha) and Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, they said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Abu Tha'labah, that he raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Khaybar while the people were hungry, and found domestic donkeys there, and the people slaughtered some of them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told, so he ordered 'Abd al-Rahman to call out among the people: The meat of domestic donkeys is for whoever does not testify that I am the Messenger of Allah. So they overturned their pots with what was in them, and they found onions and garlic in their gardens. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats of this tree should not approach us."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Plunder is not lawful, nor is every carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey lawful, nor is the tied animal lawful."""
"20071","'Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi from Abu Tha'labah. 578 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a gold ring on his hand and began tapping it with a stick he had. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked away, he threw it off. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I see we have only pained you and cost you."""
"20072","579 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Rashid narrate from al-Zuhri, from 'Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: A man sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a gold ring, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tapped his hand with a stick in his hand. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked away from him, and the man threw off his ring. He looked at him and said: ""Where is your ring?"" He said: I threw it off. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I think we have pained you and cost you."""
"20073","Abu Asma al-Rahabi from Abu Tha'labah. 580 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-'A'ishi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub and Qatadah, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma al-Rahabi, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in the land of the People of the Book; we cook in their pots and drink in their vessels. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If you find nothing else, rinse them with water."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of game; what should we do? He said: ""When you release your trained dog and mention the name of Allah, eat; and if it is untrained, slaughter and eat; and when you release your arrow and mention the name of Allah, eat."""
"20074","581 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us; (ha) and 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me, they said: Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma al-Rahabi, from Abu Tha'labah, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: We need the vessels of the polytheists on our journeys; we cook and drink in them. He said: ""Wash them with water, then cook and drink in them."""
"20075","Abu 'Ubayd Allah Muslim ibn Mishkam from Abu Tha'labah. 582 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah 'Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn al-'Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us; (ha) and Abu 'Abd al-Malik Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-'Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, my father 'Abd Allah ibn al-'Ala narrated to me, Muslim ibn Mishkam narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani say: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me what is lawful for me and what is unlawful. He raised his gaze at me and lowered it, and said: ""Nuwaybah."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, a Nuwaybah of good or a Nuwaybah of evil? He said: ""Rather a Nuwaybah of good. Do not eat the meat of the domestic donkey nor any carnivore with fangs among beasts of prey."""
"20076","583 - Abu 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-'Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Busr ibn 'Ubayd Allah, from Abu Idris, from Abu Tha'labah, with the like of that."
"20077","584 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-'Ala ibn Zabr, that Abu 'Ubayd Allah narrated to him, from Abu Tha'labah, that he informed him that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: We live beside the People of the Book, and they cook pork in their pots and drink wine in their vessels. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If you find anything else, eat and drink in it; and if you find nothing else, rinse them with water, then eat and drink in them."""
"20078","585 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zayd ibn Yahya ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn al-'Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, he said: I heard Muslim ibn Mishkam say: I heard Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani say: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of what is lawful for me and what is unlawful. He raised his gaze at me and lowered it, and said: Righteousness is what the soul finds rest in and the heart is at ease with, and sin is what the soul does not find rest in and the heart is not at ease with."
"20079","586 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us; (ha) and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, they said: Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn al-'Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, that he heard Abu 'Ubayd Allah Muslim ibn Mishkam say: Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani narrated to us, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would halt at a stopping place and encamp, the people would scatter from him into the mountain passes and valleys. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: {That is only Satan}. After that, when they halted at a stopping place, they would draw together, until you would say: If you spread a cloak over them it would cover them, or something like that."
"20080","Abu Umayyah al-Sha'bani from Abu Tha'labah. 587 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us; (ha) and 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ya'qub al-Talqani narrated to us, they said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, 'Utbah ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Jariyah al-Lakhmi narrated to us, Abu Umayyah al-Sha'bani narrated to us, he said: I came to Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani and said: O Abu Tha'labah, what do you do about this verse? He said: Which verse? I said: His saying: {O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; he who strays will not harm you when you are guided}. He said: By Allah, you have asked one well-informed about it. I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it, and he said: ""Rather enjoin good and forbid evil. Then when you see miserliness obeyed, desire followed, worldly life preferred, and every holder of an opinion admiring his own opinion, then keep to your own self and leave the affair of the multitude. For after you are days of patience; the patient one in them is like one grasping hot coals. For the worker in that time is the reward of fifty men."" And another besides 'Utbah ibn Abi Hakim added to me: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, the reward of fifty men of us or of them? He said: ""No, rather the reward of fifty men of you."""
"20081","Makhul from Abu Tha'labah. 588 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to me, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Makhul, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The most beloved of you to me and the nearest of you to me in sitting in the Hereafter are the best of you in character; and the most hateful of you to me and the farthest of you from me in the Hereafter are the worst of you in character: the babblers, the loud-mouthed, and the pompous."""
"20082","589 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Makhul, from Abu Tha'labah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah has obligated obligations, so do not neglect them; and He has forbidden things, so do not violate them; and He has set limits, so do not transgress them; and He has overlooked things without forgetfulness, so do not inquire about them."""
"20083","590 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-'Askari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Adam al-Massisi narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, from Habib ibn Suhayb, from Makhul, from Abu Tha'labah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah looks upon His servants on the night of the middle of Sha'ban and forgives the believers and gives respite to the disbelievers, and leaves the spiteful with their spite until they abandon it."""
"20084","591 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Abu Wahb, from Makhul, from Abu Tha'labah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Your religion is prophethood and mercy, then caliphate and mercy, then kingship and tyranny, then biting kingship in which fornication and silk are deemed lawful."""
"20085","'Umayr ibn Hani al-'Ansi from Abu Tha'labah. 592 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to me, from 'Umayr ibn Hani, that he informed him, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot with my bow; some of it I catch alive for slaughter, and some I do not catch alive. What of it is lawful for me and what is unlawful? And I am in the land of the People of the Book, and they eat pork in their vessels and drink wine in them; may I eat and drink in them? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his gaze at me and lowered it, then said: ""Nuwaybah."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, a Nuwaybah of good or a Nuwaybah of evil? He said: ""Rather a Nuwaybah of good."" Then he said: ""Whatever your bow returns to you and you have mentioned the name of Allah over it, eat; and if you find sufficiency without the vessels of the disbelievers, do not eat in them; and if you find no sufficiency, rinse them thoroughly with water, then eat in them."""
"20086","Habib ibn al-Muhasir ibn Habib from Abu Tha'labah. 593 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Ahwas ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Habib ibn Suhayb, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah looks upon His servants on the night of the middle of Sha'ban and forgives the believers and grants respite to the disbelievers, and leaves the spiteful with their spite until they abandon it."""
"20087","594 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, from Hakim ibn Suhayb, from Abu Tha'labah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast Sha'ban and Ramadan, joining them both together."
"20088","'Urwah ibn Ruwaym al-Lakhmi from Abu Tha'labah. 595 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Sinan narrated to us, from 'Urwah ibn Ruwaym, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from a journey, he would begin with the mosque and pray two rak'ahs in it, then go to Fatimah, then come to his wives. He returned from a journey and prayed two rak'ahs in the mosque, then came to Fatimah, and she met him at the door of the house, kissing his mouth and eyes and weeping. He said: ""What makes you weep?"" She said: I see you disheveled and weary, and your clothes worn out. He said to her: ""Do not weep, for Allah has sent your father with a matter by which Allah will admit might or humiliation into every house, mud-brick or stone or fur or hair, on the face of the earth, until it reaches where the night reaches."""
"20089","596 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Ziyad al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Ibn Sinan al-Shami, from 'Urwah ibn Ruwaym, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from a journey, he would begin in the mosque and pray two rak'ahs in it, then begin with the house of Fatimah, then come to the houses of his wives. He said: He entered upon her, and she placed her hand on his cheek and said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, your clothes have become worn out. He said: ""O Fatimah, Allah has sent your father with a matter; no house of mud-brick or fur will remain but Allah will admit might into it through your father, until it reaches where the night reaches."""
"20090","597 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Abu Farwah narrated to us, 'Urwah ibn Ruwaym al-Lakhmi narrated to me, from Abu Tha'labah, and I met him and spoke to him, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, and he said: ""Nuwaybah."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, a Nuwaybah of good or a Nuwaybah of evil? He said: No, rather a Nuwaybah of good. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I went out with an uncle of mine on a journey, and he became barefoot, and said: Lend me your sandals. I said: I will not lend them to you unless you marry me to your daughter. He said: I have married her to you. When we came to our people, he sent me my sandals and said: You have no wife with us. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no good in her for you."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed a vow to slaughter camels at an idol of the idols of ignorance. He said: ""Fulfill your vow, but do not sin against your Lord."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience, nor in severing kinship, nor in what one does not own. I said: O Messenger of Allah, silver coins are found near an inhabited village or a frequented road. He said: ""Announce them for a year; if their owner comes, hand them to him; otherwise record their string, container, and number, then enjoy them."" I said: O Prophet of Allah, silver coins are found in barren land. He said: ""In them and in buried treasure is the fifth."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, my trained dog: I release it; some of it I catch and slaughter, and some I do not catch. He said: ""Eat whatever your trained dog holds for you."" I said: O Prophet of Allah, my bow: I shoot with it and hit; some of it I catch and slaughter, and some I do not catch. He said: ""Eat whatever your bow returns to you."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot my arrow and it disappears from me, then I find it: my arrow is in it, I recognize it and do not deny it, with no other trace on it. He said: ""If you have not left it overnight and you find it with your arrow in it, and you recognize it and do not deny it, and there is no other trace on it, then eat; otherwise do not eat."" I said: O Prophet of Allah, a sheep we find in open desert land. He said: ""Eat it, for it is only for you or for your brother or for the wolf."" I said: O Prophet of Allah, a camel or she-camel found in open desert land with its container and waterskin on it. He said: ""Leave it alone; what have you to do with it?"" I said: O Prophet of Allah, the pots of the polytheists: we cook in them. He said: ""Do not cook."" I said: If we need them and find no alternative. He said: ""Then rinse them well with water, then cook and eat."""
"20091","598 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Sinan, 'Urwah ibn Ruwaym narrated to me, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""In buried treasure is the fifth."""
"20092","Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani from Abu Tha'labah. 599 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Abu Qahdham narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, that Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land whose people are People of the Book; they eat pork and drink wine, so what do you command us concerning their vessels and pots? He said: ""If you find others, take them; otherwise rinse them with water, then eat and drink in them."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, I am in a land of game. He said: ""When you release your trained dog and mention the name of Allah and it kills, eat; and when you release your untrained dog, if you catch its slaughter mention the name of Allah over it and eat; and whatever your arrow returns to you, mention the name of Allah over it and eat."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is unlawful for us? He said: ""Every beast of prey with fangs."""
"20093","Abu Raja al-'Utaridi from Abu Tha'labah. 600 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Farah, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to me, 'Ali ibn Ghurab narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu Raja al-'Utaridi narrated to me, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land whose people are People of the Book; they eat pork and drink wine. What do you command us concerning their pots and vessels? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If you find others, otherwise rinse them with water and cook and drink in them."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people of hunting; one's trained dog returns to him and his untrained dog, and one's arrow returns to him. What of that do we eat, and what do we leave? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whatever your trained dog returns to you when you have released it and mentioned the name of Allah, eat; and whatever your untrained dog returns to you, if you catch its slaughter mention the name of Allah then eat; and whatever your arrow returns to you when you have released it and mentioned the name of Allah, eat."" Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, what is not lawful for us? He said: ""The domestic donkey and every beast of prey with fangs."""
"20094","'Umar ibn Nabhan from Abu Tha'labah. 601 - 'Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us; (ha) and Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sha'tam ibn Asil narrated to us, Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from 'Umar ibn Nabhan, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: Two sons of mine died, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, two sons of mine have died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever has two sons die will be admitted by Allah into Paradise by virtue of His mercy upon them."" Abu Hurayrah met me and said: Are you the one to whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke about the two sons? I said: Yes. He said: Had he narrated it to me, it would be dearer to me than what Palestine holds."
"20095","Abu Qilabah from Abu Tha'labah. 602 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Tha'labah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Is there zakat on donkeys? He said: ""No, except for the isolated, singular verse: {So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it}."""
"20096","603 - 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we come to the land of the People of the Book, and I asked him about their vessels. He said: ""Wash them, then cook in them."""
"20097","604 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Tha'labah, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, assign me land in writing. He said: ""How shall I write when it is in the land of war?"" He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, he will surely rule what is under their feet. That pleased the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he looked at his Companions, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for him. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of game; what of it is lawful for us and what is unlawful? He said: ""When you release your trained or disciplined dog and mention Allah, and it seizes and kills, eat; and when you release your untrained dog, whatever of it you catch alive eat, and whatever you do not catch alive do not eat; and whatever your arrow returns to you, eat."" He said: O Prophet of Allah, we are in a land whose people are People of the Book; we need their pots and vessels. He said: ""Do not approach them as long as you find an alternative; if you find no alternative, wash them with water and cook and drink."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the meat of the domestic donkey and every beast of prey with fangs."
"20098","605 - 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Bursani narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to me, that Abu Qilabah narrated to him, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Our land is a land of game; I release my arrow and mention the name of Allah, and I release my trained dog and mention the name of Allah, and I release my untrained dog and mention the name of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whatever your arrow holds for you and you have mentioned the name of Allah, eat; and whatever your trained dog holds for you and you have mentioned the name of Allah, eat; and whatever your untrained dog holds for you and you catch its slaughter, eat; and if you do not catch its slaughter, do not eat."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, our land is the land of the People of the Book; what do you command us to do with their vessels? He said: ""Do not approach them unless you find no alternative; then wash them with water and cook in them."""
"20099","The chapter of ya. Those named Yazid. Yazid ibn Abi Sufyan ibn Harb ibn Umayyah ibn 'Abd Shams ibn 'Abd Manaf. 606 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Sufyan died in Sham in the year eighteen, and he had appointed Mu'awiyah as successor, and 'Umar confirmed him."""
"20100","607 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to us, that when Abu Bakr sent Yazid ibn Abi Sufyan to Sham, he went out walking with him. Yazid said to him: Either you ride, or I dismount. He said: ""I will not ride, nor will you dismount; I seek reward for my steps."""
"20101","Yazid ibn al-Aswad al-Suwa'i Abu Jabir. 608 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Hisham ibn Hassan and al-Thawri, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata al-Ta'ifi, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad, from his father, he said: We prayed Fajr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he turned and saw two men behind the people. He called them, their sinews trembling, and said: ""What prevented you from praying with the people?"" They said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed in our lodgings. He said: ""Do not do so; when one of you has prayed in his lodging then reaches the prayer with the imam, let him pray it with him, for it is voluntary for him."""
"20102","609 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Jabir ibn Yazid, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the morning prayer in the mosque of al-Khayf and saw two men after he finished in the back of the mosque. He sent for them, and they were brought with their sinews shaking. He said: ""What is the matter with you that you did not pray with us?"" They said: We had prayed in our lodgings. He said: When one of you comes to the congregation having already prayed in his house, let him pray with them, for it is voluntary for him."
"20103","610 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Ya'la ibn 'Ata narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer, and when he finished his prayer he saw two men at the back of the people. He ordered them brought, and they were brought with their sinews trembling. He said: ""What made you not pray with us?"" They said: O Prophet of Allah, we prayed in our lodgings then came. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you have prayed in your lodgings then reach the prayer, pray, for it is voluntary for you."
"20104","611 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn A'yan narrated to me, from Shu'bah, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad al-Suwa'i, from his father, he said: We prayed dawn with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina, and there were two men at the back of the mosque who had not prayed. He called them, and they were brought with their sinews trembling. He said: ""What prevented you from praying with us?"" They said: O Messenger of Allah, we had prayed in our lodgings. He said: ""Do not do so; when you have prayed in your lodgings then come to the imam before he has prayed, pray with him, for it is voluntary for you."""
"20105","612 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad al-Suwa'i, from his father, that he was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he prayed Fajr in the mosque of al-Khayf. When he finished his prayer, there were two men at the back of the mosque, and they were brought with their sinews trembling. He said: ""What is with you that you did not pray with us?"" He said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed in our lodgings then came while you were praying, so we sat. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you has prayed in his lodging then comes while the imam is praying, let him pray with him, for it is voluntary for him."
"20106","613 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad al-Suwa'i, from his father, he said: I prayed the morning prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina in the mosque of al-Khayf. When he gave the salutation, he faced the people, and there were two men at the rear of the people who had not prayed with the people. He said: ""What prevented you from praying with the people?"" They said: O Messenger of Allah, we had prayed in our lodgings. He said: Do not do so; when one of you has prayed in his lodging and reaches the prayer with the people, let him pray it with them, for it is voluntary for him."
"20107","614 - Ahmad ibn Mas'ud al-Maqdisi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad al-Suwa'i, from his father; (ha) and 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; (ha) and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Shihab ibn 'Abbad narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad, from his father, he said: I witnessed the prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque of al-Khayf. When he finished the prayer, there were two men sitting aside, and they were brought with their sinews trembling. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What prevented you from praying?"" They said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed in our lodgings. He said: When you have prayed in your lodgings and reach the prayer with the people, pray it with them; and what you prayed in your lodgings is the obligatory one."
"20108","615 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad, from his father, he said: I witnessed the Fajr prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina, and he mentioned the like of it."
"20109","616 - Abu al-Darda 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath al-Antrartusi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jami', from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad, from his father, he said: I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Farewell Pilgrimage, and prayed the morning prayer with him at Mina. When he finished his prayer, he saw two men behind the people who had not prayed with the people, and said: Bring me the two men. They were brought with their sinews trembling. He said: ""Did you not pray with us?"" They said: O Messenger of Allah, we had prayed in our lodgings, and thought we would not reach the prayer. He said: ""Do not do so; when you have prayed in your lodgings then reach the prayer, pray, and it will be voluntary for you."" One of them said: Ask forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""O Allah, forgive him."""
"20110","617 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"20111","618 - Ahmad ibn Isma'il ibn al-Harith al-'Adawi al-Basri narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad al-Suwa'i, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, give me your hand. He gave me it, and it was colder than snow and sweeter in scent than musk."
"20112","619 - Abu al-Darda 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath al-Antrartusi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah, from Ghaylan ibn Jami', from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad, from his father, he said: ""I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the people crowded around the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I was then among the youngest and strongest of men. I pushed through the people until I took the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and placed it on my chest. I never saw anything colder nor sweeter than the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"20113","620 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Wahb al-'Allaf narrated to us, Khalid ibn 'Amr al-Umawi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad, from his father, he said: I recited to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one hundred rhymes of the poetry of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt; each time I passed a verse, he said: ""Go on."" And I heard him say in that gathering: The neighbor is most entitled to his adjoining property."
"20114","Yazid Abu Ma'n al-Sulami. 621 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Muhammad al-'Anqazi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu al-Juwayriyah, whose name is Hittan ibn Khufaf, Ma'n ibn Yazid narrated to me, he said: My father Yazid went out with dinars to give in charity and handed them to me, saying: Hand them to a man of the people of the mosque. I handed them to other than him, then came to my father and informed him. He said: That is not what I intended. I disputed with him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""For you, O Ma'n, is what you took; and for you, O Yazid, is what you intended."""
"20115","Yazid ibn 'Amir al-Suwa'i. 622 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from his father al-Sa'ib ibn Yasar, from Yazid ibn 'Amir al-Suwa'i, he said: At a rout in which the Muslims were routed on the day of Hunayn, the disbelievers pursued them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a handful of earth and threw it at their faces, saying: ""Return; may the faces be disfigured."" There was none of us who met his brother but he was complaining of specks and wiping his eyes."
"20116","623 - And from Yazid ibn 'Amir, and he had witnessed Hunayn with the polytheists then accepted Islam, he said: We asked him about the terror Allah cast into their hearts on the day of Hunayn, how it was. He took a pebble and threw it at a basin, and it rang. He said: ""We used to find in our bellies the like of that."""
"20117","624 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us; (ha) and 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, they said: Ma'n ibn 'Isa narrated to us, Sa'id ibn al-Sa'ib al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from Nuh ibn Sa'sa'ah, from Yazid ibn 'Amir, he said: I came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in prayer, either in Zuhr or in 'Asr, and I had prayed them at home. When I found the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer, I sat and did not join them in prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to us and saw me sitting, and said: ""Have you not accepted Islam, O Yazid?"" I said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah, I have accepted Islam. He said: ""What prevents you from joining the people in their prayer?"" I said: I had prayed at home, and I thought you had already prayed. He said: When you come to the prayer and find the people praying, pray with them; even if you have already prayed, it will be voluntary for you and this is obligatory."
"20118","Yazid ibn Asad ibn Kurz al-Bajali al-Qasri. 625 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Awn narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, he said: I heard Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah al-Qasri narrate from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Yazid, love for people what you love for yourself."""
"20119","Yazid ibn al-Akhnas al-Sulami. 626 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Yazid ibn al-Akhnas, and he was a Companion: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no rivalry among you except in two: a man to whom Allah has given the Qur'an and he stands with it through the hours of night and day, or follows what is in it, and a man says: Had Allah given me what He gave so-and-so, I would stand with it as he stands with it; and a man to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends and gives charity, and a man says the like of that."""
"20120","Yazid ibn Thabit al-Ansari, brother of Zayd ibn Thabit, a participant at Badr. 627 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; (ha) and Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn Zayd informed me, from his uncle Yazid ibn Thabit, that they went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day with a funeral, until when they reached al-Baqi', he said: ""What is this?"" They said: This is so-and-so, a freedwoman of such-and-such family, and he recognized her. He said: ""Why did you not inform me of her?"" They said: We buried her at noon, and you were taking your midday rest asleep, and we did not wish to trouble you. He stood and arranged the people behind him and said takbir over her four times, then said: ""None of you should die while I am among you but you inform me, for my prayer for him is a mercy."""
"20121","628 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his uncle Yazid ibn Thabit, and he was older than Zayd, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when we reached al-Baqi' there was a new grave. He asked about it, and they said: So-and-so, and he recognized her. He said: ""Did you not inform me?"" They said: You were taking your midday rest fasting, and we disliked troubling you. He said: Do not do so; let me never know that one of you has died while I am among you but you inform me, for my prayer over him is a mercy for him. Then he came to the grave and we lined up behind him, and he said takbir over it four times."
"20122","629 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from his uncle Yazid ibn Thabit, that he: ""was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions, when a funeral appeared. When he saw it, he stood and his Companions stood, and they remained standing until it had passed far. By Allah, I do not know whether from its harm or from the narrowness of the place, and I think it was only the funeral of a Jew or Jewess, and we did not ask him about his standing."""
"20123","630 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from his grandfather, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""None of you should take the belongings of his brother, neither in jest nor in earnest; and when one of you takes his brother's staff, let him return it."""
"20124","631 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Hashim ibn 'Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, from his father, ""that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated and raised his hands, he would wipe his face with his hands."""
"20125","632 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Shabbah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Raja al-Makki narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us extra spoils besides our share of the fifth, and I received an old she-camel."
"20126","Yazid ibn Salamah al-Ju'fi. 633 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from Ibn Ashwa', from Yazid ibn Salamah al-Ju'fi, he said: Yazid said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I have heard much hadith from you, and I fear the first of it will make me forget the last of it, so tell me a word that will be comprehensive. He said: ""Fear Allah in what you know."""
"20127","634 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Muhammad al-'Anqazi narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Alqamah ibn Wa'il, from Yazid ibn Salamah al-Ju'fi, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what if there are rulers over us who take the right due to them and withhold the right due to us? Al-Ash'ath said to him: Sit down. He repeated it a second then a third time. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Upon them is what they were charged with, and upon you is what you were charged with."""
"20128","Yazid ibn Qatadah. 635 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, 'Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us; (ha) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us; (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Hassan ibn Bilal, that Yazid ibn Qatadah narrated that a man of his family died upon other than Islam. He said: My sister inherited him to my exclusion, and she was upon his religion. Then my father accepted Islam and was present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Hunayn and died, so I secured his inheritance, and he had left a slave boy and palm trees. Then my sister accepted Islam and disputed with me over the inheritance before 'Uthman. 'Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam narrated to him that 'Umar ruled that whoever accepts Islam over an inheritance before it is divided gets his share. So 'Uthman ruled with it, and she took that first one and shared with me in this; and the wording is that of the hadith of Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani."
"20129","Yazid Abu 'Abd al-Rahman. 636 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri; (ha) and 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn 'Ubayd Allah, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the Farewell Pilgrimage: ""Your slaves, your slaves: feed them of what you eat and clothe them of what you wear; and if they come with a sin you do not wish to forgive, then sell the servants of Allah and do not torment them."""
"20130","Yazid ibn Nu'amah al-Dabbi, and there is disagreement over his Companionship. 637 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from 'Imran al-Qasir, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Nu'amah al-Dabbi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a man befriends a man, let him ask him about his name and his father's name and from whom he is, for it is a stronger bond of affection."""
"20131","Yazid Abu 'Umar. 638 - Ahmad ibn al-Fadl al-'Askari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Raja al-Harrani narrated to us, Khattab ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Yazid, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There is no one who kills a sparrow but it will cry out on the Day of Resurrection, saying: O Lord, this one killed me heedlessly; he neither benefited from killing me nor left me to live in Your earth."""
"20132","Yazid ibn Husayn al-Sulami. 639 - 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Salih al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Faraj, the neighbor of Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn 'Ulayy ibn Rabah informed me, he said: I heard my father mention, from Yazid ibn Husayn al-Sulami, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is Saba? Was he a prophet or a woman? He said: ""Rather a man of the Arabs."" He said: What did he beget? He said: ""He begot ten: six settled in Yemen, and four in Sham. Those in Yemen: Kindah, Madhhij, al-Azd, al-Ash'ariyyun, Anmar, and Himyar; and in Sham: Lakhm, Judham, 'Amilah, and Ghassan."""
"20133","Yazid ibn Ma'bad al-Hanafi. 640 - Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Zaybaqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Miskin al-Yamami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn 'Utbah, from Ma'bad ibn Yazid, from his father, Yazid ibn Ma'bad, he said: I came as a delegate to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he asked me about Yamamah: ""Among whom is the multitude of its people?"" I wanted to say: Among Banu 'Abd Allah ibn al-Du'al, then I disliked lying to the Prophet of Allah, so I said: The multitude of them is among Banu 'Ubayd. He said: ""You have spoken truthfully; a land that grew upon hardship, and its people will not perish."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, why is that? He said: ""Because they work with their hands and eat with their slaves."""
"20134","Yazid ibn Shajarah. 641 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq; (ha) and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad ibn Hassan al-Mu'addib narrated to us, both from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Yazid ibn Shajarah, and Yazid ibn Shajarah was one whose word and deed were deemed truthful, he said: He addressed us and said: O people, remember the blessing of Allah upon you; how good is the blessing of Allah upon you, seen among green and yellow and red, and in the lodgings is what is in them. And he used to say: When people line up for prayer and line up for battle, the doors of heaven are opened, and the doors of Paradise, and the doors of Hell, and the houris are adorned and look out. When a man advances, they say: O Allah, help him; and when he retreats, they veil themselves from him and say: O Allah, forgive him. So strike hard at the faces of the enemy, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, and do not disgrace the houris. For the first drop that drips of his blood expiates for him everything he did, and two wives of the houris descend upon him, wiping the dust from his face and saying: Now it is time for us; and he says: Now it is time for us. Then he is clothed with one hundred robes, not of the weaving of the children of Adam, but of the growth of Paradise; were one placed between his fingers it would fit. And he used to say: I have been told that swords are the keys of Paradise; and the wording is that of 'Abd al-Samad ibn Hassan."
"20135","642 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Fahd ibn 'Awf Abu Rabi'ah narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Yazid ibn Shajarah, that he said: O people, the world has come to morning and evening among green and red and yellow, and in the houses is what is in them. When you meet the enemy, then forward, forward: for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No man advances a step in the path of Allah but the houris look out to him; and if he retreats, they are shy of him and veil themselves from him. If he is martyred, the first gash of his blood is an expiation for his sins, and two of the houris descend to him, shaking the dust from his face and saying: Welcome, now it is time for you; and he says: Welcome to you."""
"20136","Yazid ibn Zam'ah al-Qurashi al-Asadi, martyred with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn. 643 - Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah, in naming those martyred on the day of Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of Quraysh, of Banu Asad ibn 'Abd al-'Uzza: Yazid ibn Zam'ah. So said Ibn Lahi'ah, and in my view it is a mistake."
"20137","644 - Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, in naming those martyred on the day of Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of Quraysh, then of Banu Asad: Yazid ibn Zam'ah ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib; a horse of his called al-Janah bolted with him and killed him."
"20138","645 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, in naming those martyred on the day of Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of Quraysh, then of Banu Asad: Yazid ibn Zam'ah."
"20139","Yazid ibn Sayf ibn Jariyah al-Yarbu'i. 646 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Yusuf al-Qulusi narrated to us; (ha) and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah and Ahmad ibn Ma Bihram al-Idhaji narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, they said: al-Salt ibn Muhammad Abu Hammam al-Kharaki narrated to us, Mawdud ibn al-Harith ibn Yazid ibn Sayf ibn Jariyah al-Yarbu'i narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man of Banu Tamim has taken all my wealth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""I have no wealth to give you."" Then he said: ""Would you like to be appointed over your people?"" I said: No. He said: ""Indeed the headman is thrust into the Fire with a thrust."""
"20140","Yazid ibn Rukanah ibn 'Abd Yazid ibn Hashim, who died in the caliphate of Mu'awiyah. 647 - Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, Husayn ibn Zayd ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Yazid ibn Rukanah, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the dead, he would say takbir four times then say: ""O Allah, Your servant and the son of Your maidservant is in need of Your mercy, and You are in no need of his torment. If he was a doer of good, increase in his good; and if he was a doer of evil, overlook him."" Then he would supplicate with whatever Allah willed him to supplicate."
"20141","Those named Ya'la. Ya'la ibn Umayyah al-Tamimi, ally of Banu Nawfal ibn 'Abd Manaf, and he is Ya'la ibn Umayyah ibn Abi 'Ubaydah ibn Hammam ibn al-Harith ibn Bakr ibn Zayd ibn Malik ibn Zayd Manat ibn Tamim, and his mother is Munyah bint Ghazwan al-Sulamiyyah, sister of 'Utbah ibn Ghazwan. What Ya'la ibn Umayyah transmitted. Safwan ibn Ya'la, from his father. 648 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from 'Ata, he said: Safwan ibn Ya'la ibn Umayyah informed me, from Ya'la ibn Umayyah, he said: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of hardship, and Ya'la used to say: That expedition is my most firmly trusted deed with me. I had a hireling, and he fought a man, and one of them bit the other; the bitten one pulled his hand from the biter's mouth, pulling out one of his front teeth. They came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he voided his tooth. I think he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Would he leave his hand in your mouth for you to chomp it as if in the mouth of a stallion, chomping it?"""
"20142","649 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from 'Ata, from Safwan ibn Ya'la, from his father, he said: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk on a difficult young camel, and it was my most firmly trusted deed in myself. I hired a hireling, and my hireling fought a man and bit his hand, pulling out his tooth. He disputed with him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he voided it, saying: ""Would you leave his hand in your mouth for you to chomp it like the chomping of a stallion?"""
"20143","650 - 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Badr al-Basri narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Dinar and Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from 'Ata, from Safwan ibn Ya'la, from his father, he said: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk on a difficult young camel, with a hireling of mine. My hireling fought a man and bit him, and he pulled his hand from his mouth, and his tooth fell out. He was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to him: ""Would you leave his hand in your mouth for you to chomp it as a stallion chomps?"" And he voided it."
"20144","651 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; (ha) and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us; (ha) and 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Ya'la ibn Munyah, from his father, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having bitten the hand of a man; he pulled his hand away and the tooth of the one who bit him fell out. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nullified it and said: ""Did you want to chomp it as a stallion chomps?"""
"20145","652 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-'Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah; (ha) and Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya, the scribe of al-'Umari, narrated to us, he said: Rishdin narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Khalid ibn Kathir al-Hamdani, from 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Safwan ibn Ya'la, from his father and his uncle Salamah ibn Umayyah, that they went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk, with a companion of ours. A man of the people fought him and bit him, and our companion pulled his hand from his mouth, knocking out part of his mouth. He went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked for blood-money. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""One of you goes to his brother and bites him with the bite of a stallion, then comes asking for blood-money?"" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) voided it."
"20146","A chapter. 653 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; (ha) and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, they said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah say: Safwan ibn Ya'la ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from his father, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at al-Ji'ranah, wearing a cloak with traces of khaluq on it - Hammam said: Or he said: traces of saffron-yellow - and said: How do you command me to do in my 'Umrah? He said: Revelation was sent down upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was screened with a garment. He said: And Ya'la used to say: I wished I had seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when revelation was being sent to him. 'Umar said to me: Would you like to look at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while revelation has been sent down upon him? He lifted the edge of the garment and I looked at him, and he was snorting - Hammam said: I think he also said: Like the snorting of a young camel. When it was lifted from him, he said: ""Where is the questioner about 'Umrah? Take off the cloak and wash off yourself either the traces of khaluq, or the traces of saffron-yellow - Hammam doubted - and do in your 'Umrah what you did in your Hajj."""
"20147","654 - Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-'Attar al-Basri narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from 'Ata, from Safwan ibn Ya'la, from his father Ya'la, he said: I said to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab: I wish I had seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when revelation came down upon him. He said: We were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he halted at a stopping place, and a Bedouin came to him wearing a cloak with saffron on it, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have entered ihram for 'Umrah, and the people mock me; how should I do? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept silent toward him, and Allah sent down revelation. 'Umar signaled to me with his hand, and I put my head into the tent, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was red in his eyes and forehead. It was lifted from him, and he said: ""Where is the questioner about 'Umrah?"" He said: I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""Remove your cloak from you, and whatever you would do in your Hajj, do in your 'Umrah."""
"20148","655 - Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-'Attar narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrahim al-Zuhri narrated to us, my uncle narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Safwan ibn Ya'la ibn Umayyah, from his father, he said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were with him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have entered ihram, wearing perfume and a woolen cloak and a turban. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Remove your turban and your shirt, and wash this yellow off yourself; and whatever you would do in your Hajj, do in your 'Umrah."""
"20149","656 - Yusuf al-Qadi and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Dinar and Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Safwan ibn Ya'la ibn Umayyah, from his father, he said: I said to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab: I love to see the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when revelation comes down upon him. When we were at al-Ji'ranah, revelation was sent down upon him, and a garment was drawn over him. 'Umar called me and uncovered the garment from his face for me, and I saw him snorting with his face red. Before that, a Bedouin had come to him wearing sewn garments, scented with khaluq, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have entered ihram for 'Umrah wearing this; how do you command me to do? He did not answer him with anything until revelation was sent down upon him. When it was lifted from him, he said: ""Where is the questioner?"" He said: Here I am. He said: ""What if you were in ihram for Hajj wearing this, how would you do?"" He said: I would remove these sewn garments from me and wash this khaluq off me. He said: ""Then go and remove these sewn garments from you, and wash this khaluq off you, and do in your 'Umrah as you would do in your Hajj."""
"20150","657 - Yusuf al-Qadi and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata, from Safwan ibn Ya'la, from his father, he said: I said to 'Umar: I love to see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when revelation comes down upon him, with the like of the hadith of 'Amr ibn Dinar."
"20151","658 - Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Sarraj al-Qadi narrated to us, al-Sakan ibn Sa'id al-Qadi narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Qays ibn Sa'd narrate, from 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Safwan ibn Ya'la, from his father, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Ji'ranah, wearing a cloak, with his beard and head yellowed with dye, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have entered ihram as you see me. He said: ""Wash the yellow off yourself and remove the cloak from you; and whatever you would do in your Hajj, do in your 'Umrah."""
"20152","659 - Isma'il ibn Qirat al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to me, he said: Safwan ibn Ya'la ibn Umayyah informed me, that his father informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by al-Ji'ranah when he came from Hunayn, distributing their spoils, and a Bedouin came to him wearing a shirt or cloak, having dyed himself yellow, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have entered ihram for 'Umrah; what do you think? He did not reply to him with anything. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) withdrew for revelation, and 'Umar stood screening him with his garment. Ya'la ibn Munabbih said: I love to see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when revelation is sent to him. 'Umar called him and he put his head under the garment and found him snorting like one asleep. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose and called the Bedouin, ordering him to remove his cloak and shirt, and said to him: ""Wash, and wear the waist-wrapper and cloak, and do in your 'Umrah what you do in your Hajj."""
"20153","660 - Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Khatib al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Hafs ibn 'Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Rabah ibn Abi Ma'ruf narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah say: Safwan ibn Ya'la informed me, from his father, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man came to him wearing a cloak with traces of khaluq on it, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have entered ihram for 'Umrah; how should I do? He kept silent toward him and did not reply. 'Umar would screen him with a shade when revelation came down upon him. I said to 'Umar: I love, when revelation comes down upon him, to put my head with him in the garment. When it was sent down, 'Umar covered him with the garment, and I came and put my head with him in the garment and looked at him. When it was lifted from him, he said: ""Where is the one who just asked about 'Umrah?"" The man stood up to him, and he said: Remove your cloak from you, and wash off the traces of khaluq on you, and do in your 'Umrah what you would do in your Hajj."
"20154","'Uthman ibn Ya'la ibn Umayyah from his father. 661 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, Abu 'Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Mihran narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Uthman ibn Ya'la ibn Umayyah narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, he said: While we were traveling one day with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), there was a camel. When it saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it raised its head toward him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Ya'la, go to the owners of this camel and buy it from them; and if they do not sell to you, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoins you concerning it."" They said: By Allah, we have watered with it for twenty years, and we intended to slaughter it in the morning; but since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has enjoined us concerning it, we will not fall short in good toward it."
"20155","662 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Sa'id al-Jarmi narrated to us, Abu 'Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Mihran narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Uthman ibn Ya'la ibn Umayyah narrated to us, that his father narrated to him, from his grandfather, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey one day, there were three scattered lote trees. He said: ""O Ya'la, go to these lote trees and say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to gather by Allah's permission."" They walked until they came together into one root, and he screened himself with them for some need. Then he said: ""O Ya'la, go to them and order them to return by Allah's permission."" They walked until each one returned to its place."
"20156","663 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Dawud ibn 'Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Rammah, the judge of Balkh, narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Ziyad al-Azdi Abu Sahl narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Uthman ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, and rain befell us; there was wetness beneath us and rain from above us, and we were in a narrow pass, and the prayer came. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal, and he called the adhan and the iqamah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went forward and prayed upon his mount, and the people were upon their mounts, gesturing with gestures, making the prostration lower than the bowing."""
"20157","664 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from 'Amr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Umayyah, from his father, that he informed him that Ya'la ibn Umayyah informed him that he brought his father to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of the Conquest, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, pledge my father upon hijrah (emigration). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Rather, I pledge him upon jihad, for hijrah has ended after the Conquest."""
"20158","665 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Numayr al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Ufayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from 'Uqayl, and Rushdin, from 'Uqayl and Qurrah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Amr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'la ibn Umayyah, that his father informed him that Ya'la said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, pledge my father upon hijrah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I pledge him upon jihad, for hijrah has ended."""
"20159","Mujahid from Ya'la ibn Umayyah. 666 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, that Ya'la ibn Umayyah fought a man, and one of them bit the hand of his companion, so he pulled his hand from his mouth and knocked out his front tooth. So he disputed with him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""Does one of you bite his brother as the young camel bites?"" So he annulled it (awarded no compensation). Al-Hakam said to me: Do you know what 'he annulled it' means? I said: Yes. He said: So he voided it."
"20160","Khalid ibn al-Durayk from Ya'la. 667 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, from Bashir ibn Talhah, he said: I heard Khalid ibn al-Durayk say: I heard Ya'la ibn Munabbih say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an expedition, and a man used to go out with me on expeditions. When that expedition came, he said: I will not go out with you until you assign something for me. So I assigned him three dinars. When it came to the shares (of booty), I said: There is no share for you. So I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""Those three dinars are his portion of the Hereafter and this world. As for something they exchange among themselves, it is not like that."""
"20161","668 - Al-Hasan ibn Sufyan al-Saffar al-Massisi and 'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi said: Sulaym ibn Mansur ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Bashir ibn Talhah al-Judhami narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Durayk, from Ya'la ibn Munabbih, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The Fire will say to the believer on the Day of Resurrection: Pass, O believer, for your light has extinguished my flame."""
"20162","Rest of the hadith of Safwan ibn Ya'la from his father. 669 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, (h), and Mahmud ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Rahmawayh narrated to us, they said: Hushaim narrated to us, Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, 'Abd al-Malik, al-Hajjaj and Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from 'Ata, from Ya'la ibn Munabbih, he said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a jubbah (cloak) with traces of khaluq (perfume) on it, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have entered ihram as you see, and the people mock me. So he turned away from him in silence for a while, then said: ""Wash this saffron off yourself, take off your jubbah, and do in your 'umrah as you would do in your hajj."" And they did not mention Safwan ibn Ya'la in the hadith."
"20163","670 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-A'raj narrated to us, (h), and al-'Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Sa'iqah narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from 'Ata, from Safwan ibn Ya'la, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O people, Allah is Modest and Generous; when one of you bathes, let him cover himself."""
"20164","671 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Ata, from Safwan ibn Ya'la, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon the minbar: {And they will call: O Malik, let your Lord put an end to us}."
"20165","Ya'la ibn Murrah al-Thaqafi. 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'la ibn Murrah from his father. 'Umar ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'la from his father from his grandfather. 672 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'la ibn Murrah, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I saw three things from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that no one saw before me: I was with him on the road to Makkah, and he passed a woman with a son of hers afflicted with madness, the severest madness I had ever seen. She said: O Messenger of Allah, this son of mine is as you see. He said: If you wish, I will supplicate for him. So he supplicated for him, then went on. A camel passed stretching its neck, bellowing. He said: Bring me the owner of this. So he came, and he said: This says: I was born among them, and they used me until I grew old, and when I grew old they wanted to slaughter me. Then he went on and saw two trees apart from each other, and said to me: Go and order them to join together. So they joined, and he relieved himself, and said: Go and tell them to separate. Then he went on, and when he returned he passed the boy playing with the boys, and his mother had prepared six rams and gifted him two rams, and said: Nothing of the madness has returned to him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing except that it knows that I am the Messenger of Allah, except the disbelieving and rebellious among the jinn and mankind."
"20166","673 - 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, 'Umar ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'la ibn Murrah al-Thaqafi narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: When we traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we would not remove our khuffs (leather socks) for three (days); and when we were resident, then for a day and a night."
"20167","674 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sahl ibn Zanjalah al-Razi narrated to us, al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'la ibn Murrah al-Thaqafi, from his father, from his grandfather, and from Ziyad ibn 'Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding wiping over the khuffs: ""For the traveler three (days), and for the resident a day and a night."""
"20168","675 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sahl ibn Zanjalah said: al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'la ibn Murrah, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."""
"20169","676 - Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Asbahani narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maslamah al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Zuhayr 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'la, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Three things Allah, Mighty and Exalted, loves: hastening the breaking of the fast, delaying the suhur (pre-dawn meal), and striking the hands, one with the other, in prayer."""
"20170","677 - Abu 'Amir Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Nahwi said: Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Ibn Ya'la, from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a gold ring in my hand, and he said: ""Do you pay the zakat of this?"" I said: No. He said: ""A great ember."""
"20171","678 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Imran al-Thaqafi, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a gold ring upon him and said: ""Do you purify it (pay its zakat)?"" He said: And what is its purification? He said: ""An ember."""
"20172","Al-Minhal ibn 'Amr from Ibn Ya'la ibn Murrah. 679 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn 'Isa narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, he said: Ibn Ya'la ibn Murrah narrated to me, from his father, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I saw three wondrous things from him. He said: We alighted in a land with many trees, and he said to me: ""Go to those two trees and say to them: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to join together."" So I went to them and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to join together, and they joined. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) relieved himself, and said: ""Go and tell them to separate."" So I told them and they separated. And a woman came with a boy and said: O Messenger of Allah, this one is seized with fits seven times in the month. He said: ""Bring him near me."" So he spat in his mouth and said: ""Come out, enemy of Allah; I am the Messenger of Allah."" Then he said to her: ""When you return, inform me of what he did."" When he returned, she met him with two rams and some ghee and dried curd. He said to me: ""Take one of the two rams and what is with it."" She said: O Messenger of Allah, I have not seen that (fit) from him. He said: Then a camel came, and he saw its eyes flowing (with tears). He said: ""Whose is this?"" They said: It belongs to such-and-such family. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to them and said: ""What is the matter of this camel complaining of you?"" They said: He was our water-carrying camel, then he grew old and we wanted to slaughter him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Leave him among the camels."" So they left him."
"20173","680 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhadir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, he said: ""I saw three things from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" And he mentioned similar to it."
"20174","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq from 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'la from his father. 681 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, the brother of Hajjaj, narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'la ibn Murrah al-Thaqafi narrated to me, from his father, he said: One day I applied depilatory paste, then I perfumed myself with khaluq (a scented mixture). So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and extended my hand to him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate for me. He said: ""What is this that is upon your hand?"" I said: I applied depilatory paste then perfumed myself with khaluq. He said: ""Have you a wife?"" I said: No. He said: ""Have you a concubine?"" I said: No. He said: ""Go and wash it off, then wash it off"" - three times."
"20175","'Amr ibn Dinar from Ibn Ya'la from his father. 682 - Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, Mihran ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-A'la, from Abu Sahl al-Azdi, he said: 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated to me, from 'Imran ibn Ya'la, from Ya'la, he said: ""An obligatory prayer came while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us, and he did not go ahead of us."" I said to Abu Sahl: What called him to that? He said: The place was narrow."
"20176","'Abd Allah ibn Hafs ibn Abi 'Aqil, and there is disagreement over his name, from Ya'la ibn Murrah. 683 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Suyuti narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Hafs ibn 'Umar, from Ya'la ibn Murrah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a trace of khaluq (scented mixture) upon him, and said: ""Wash this off yourself."""
"20177","684 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Warqa ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from 'Abd Allah ibn Hafs ibn Abi 'Aqil, Ya'la ibn Murrah informed us, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me while I was perfumed with khaluq, and said: ""O Ya'la, have you a wife?"" I said: No. He said: ""Go and wash it, then wash it from yourself, then wash it from yourself, then do not return."" He said: So I went and washed it, then washed it, then washed it, then I did not return until this hour."
"20178","685 - Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib informed us, from Hafs ibn 'Abd Allah, from Ya'la ibn Murrah: that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with yellowness of saffron upon him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Wash this off yourself, then wash it, then do not return."" He said: So he washed it and did not return."
"20179","686 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from 'Abd Allah ibn Hafs, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"20180","687 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from 'Abd Allah ibn Hafs, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, he said: I passed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was perfumed with khaluq, and he said: ""O Ya'la, have you a wife?"" I said: No. He said: ""Go and wash it, then wash it, then wash it, then do not return."" He said: So I washed it, then washed it, then washed it, then I did not return."
"20181","688 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from 'Abd Allah ibn Hafs, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, he said: I passed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was perfumed with saffron, and he said: ""O Ya'la, have you a wife?"" I said: No. He said: ""Go and wash it, then wash it, then wash it, then do not return."" He said: So I went and washed it, then washed it, then washed it, then I did not return."
"20182","689 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Ibn Ya'la ibn Murrah, from his grandfather Ya'la: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in prayer, and I went to a sister of mine and smeared my face with something of khaluq. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed, he wiped their faces and left me. So it was said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left you only because of the khaluq upon your face. So I went to a well among the wells of Madinah and fell into it (washed). When the next prayer came, I came to him and he wiped my face, then said: ""The boy has returned with the good of his religion."""
"20183","Ayman ibn Thabit Abu Thabit from Ya'la. 690 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Ya'qub narrated to us, Abu Thabit narrated to me, from Ya'la ibn Murrah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes something from the land unjustly will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying its soil to the gathering place."""
"20184","691 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam and 'Abdan ibn Ahmad said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Abu Ya'fur, from Ayman, he said: I heard Ya'la al-Thaqafi say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever takes land without right will be charged to carry its soil to the gathering place."""
"20185","692 - 'Ubayd and 'Abdan said: Abu Bakr narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from al-Rabi' ibn 'Abd Allah, from Ayman ibn Thabit, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Any man who wrongs a handspan of land, Allah will charge him to bring it until it reaches the last of the seven earths, then it will be hung around his neck on the Day of Resurrection until judgment is passed among the people."""
"20186","693 - Hafs ibn 'Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, (h), and Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Uthman al-Kilabi narrated to us, (h), and Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Zurarah narrated to us, they said: 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Thabit Ayman, from Ya'la ibn Murrah al-Thaqafi, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever steals a handspan of land, or produce, will come carrying it on the Day of Resurrection to the lowest of the earths."""
"20187","'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz from Ya'la. 694 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: ""Give me this camel as a gift, or sell it to me."" He said: It is yours, O Messenger of Allah. So he branded it with the brand of charity, then sent it forth."
"20188","Musa al-Taghlibi from Ya'la ibn Murrah. 695 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ayyub al-Sukkari narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Jabir, from Musa al-Taghlibi, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever wrongs a handspan of land, and what is above it, will be charged to carry it on the Day of Resurrection until it reaches the water, then he will carry it to the gathering place."""
"20189","'Iyad Abu Ashras al-Sulami from Ya'la ibn Murrah. 696 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'la, from 'Iyad Abu Ashras al-Sulami, he said: I saw Ya'la ibn Murrah; he was invited to a feast and sat fasting, and the people were eating and he did not taste. So I said to him: By Allah, had we known you were fasting, we would not have blamed you. He said: Do not say that, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Answer your brother, for you stand with him in one of two positions: either good, and you most deserve to have witnessed it; or other than it, and you forbid him from it and command him to good."""
"20190","'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib from Ya'la ibn Murrah. 697 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Do not mutilate the servants of Allah."""
"20191","698 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Warqa ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from more than one of Thaqif, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not mutilate the servants of Allah."""
"20192","699 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from some people of his tribe, from Ya'la ibn Murrah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not mutilate My servants."""
"20193","Hikmah, the wife of Ya'la, from Ya'la ibn Murrah. 700 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'la ibn Murrah, it was narrated to him, from his grandmother Hikmah, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever picks up a small lost item, a garment or its like, let him announce it for three days; and whoever picks up more than that, six days. If its owner comes, well and good; otherwise let him give it in charity. If its owner comes, let him inform him."""
"20194","Ya'la ibn Murrah al-'Amiri. 701 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we were invited to food, and Husayn was playing in the road. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened ahead of the people, then spread his hands, and Husayn would run now here and now there, laughing with him, until he took him. Then he placed one of his hands on his chin and the other between his head and his ears, then embraced him and kissed him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Husayn is from me, and I am from him. May Allah love whoever loves him. Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are two grandsons among the grandsons."""
"20195","702 - Abu Zur'ah 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Wahb ibn Khalid narrated to us, (h), and 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Abi Rashid, that Ya'la ibn Murrah informed him, that they went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to food they were invited to, and Husayn was playing with children in the lane. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced him ahead of the people, and clasped his hands; the boy began to fall now here and now there, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed with him until he took him. Then he placed one of his hands beneath his chin and the other on the crown of his head, then held him close and kissed him, and said: ""Husayn is from me, and I am from Husayn. May Allah love whoever loves Husayn. Husayn is a grandson among the grandsons."""
"20196","703 - Abu Zur'ah 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Wuhaib narrated to us, (h), and 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, they said: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Rashid, that Ya'la ibn Murrah informed him, that he saw Hasan and Husayn coming walking to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When one of them came, he placed his hand on his neck, then the other came and he placed his other hand on his neck. Then he kissed this one, then kissed this one, then said: ""O Allah, I love them both, so love them. O people, the child is a cause of miserliness and cowardice."""
"20197","704 - 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn 'Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Rashid, that Ya'la ibn Murrah informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The last treading that the Lord of the worlds trod was in Wajj."""
"20198","Ya'la ibn Siyabah. 705 - Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, (h), and Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-'Abbadani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, (h), and 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, (h), and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu 'Umar al-Darir narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Habib ibn Abi Jubayrah, from Ya'la ibn Siyabah, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he went for his need. Two valleys came and one joined the other, and a talhah tree or a samurah tree came and encircled him, then returned to its place of growth. He said: And a camel came dragging its neck along the ground, bellowing, until what was around it became wet from its tears. He said to his Companions: ""Do you know what it says?"" They said: And what does it say? He said: ""Its owners intended to slaughter it."" So he sent to it and said: ""Will you gift it to me?"" He said: I have no wealth more beloved to me than it. He said: ""Then treat it kindly."" He said: No doubt, by Allah, I shall honor it forever. Then he came upon two graves whose occupants were being punished, and said: ""They are being punished for a matter not grave."" And he took two moist palm stalks and placed them upon their graves, then said: ""Perhaps it will be lightened for them so long as they remain moist."""
"20199","Yasar ibn 'Abd Abu 'Azzah al-Hudhali. 706 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Malih, from Abu 'Azzah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When Allah intends to take the soul of a servant in a land, He makes for him a need to go to it."""
"20200","707 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, 'Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu al-Malih, from a man of his tribe who had companionship (with the Prophet), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When Allah intends to take the soul of a servant in a land, He makes for him a need in it."""
"20201","708 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Wuhaib narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Malih, from a man of his tribe, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When Allah intends to take the soul of a servant in a land, He makes for him a need in it."""
"20202","Those named Ya'ish. Ya'ish al-Juhani, known as Dhu al-Ghurrah. 709 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother 'Isa, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ya'ish al-Juhani, known as Dhu al-Ghurrah: that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Should I perform ablution from camel meat? He said: ""Yes."" He said: Should I pray in their resting places? He said: ""No."" He said: Should I perform ablution from sheep meat? He said: ""No."" He said: Should I pray in their folds? He said: ""Yes."""
"20203","Ya'ish al-Ghifari. 710 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Ya'ish al-Ghifari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a she-camel one day and said: ""Who will milk her?"" A man said: I. He said: ""What is your name?"" He said: Murrah. He said: ""Sit down."" Then another stood, and he said: ""What is your name?"" He said: Murrah. He said: ""Sit down."" Then another stood, and he said: ""What is your name?"" He said: Jamrah. He said: ""Sit down."" Then Ya'ish stood, and he said: ""What is your name?"" He said: Ya'ish. He said: ""Milk her."""
"20204","Yasir ibn Suwayd al-Juhani. 711 - 'Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Khuza'i al-Ahwazi narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Dawud ibn Dilhath ibn Isma'il ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Musri' ibn Yasir ibn Suwayd al-Juhani, the Companion of the Prophet, narrated to us, he said: My father Dawud narrated to me, from his father Dilhath, from his father Isma'il, from his father 'Abd Allah, from his father Musri', from his father Yasir ibn Suwayd: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him with cavalry or an expedition while his wife was pregnant, and a child was born to him. His mother carried him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this child has been born, and his father is with the cavalry, so name him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took him and passed his hand over him and said: ""O Allah, multiply their men and lessen their days, and do not make them needy, nor show their young poverty."" And he said: ""Name him Musri', for he has hastened in Islam."""
"20205","Those named Yathribi. Yathribi, and it is said: Yathribi ibn 'Awf Abu Rimthah al-Taymi, Taym al-Ribab. There is disagreement over his name: it is said Habib ibn Habban ibn 'Amir ibn 'Abd Qays, and it is said Habban ibn Wahb, and it is said Rifa'ah ibn Yathribi. 712 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr say: Abu Rimthah is Habib ibn Habban."
"20206","713 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Rimthah, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while people of Rabi'ah were disputing over blood-money, and he was saying: ""The upper hand is better than the lower hand: your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, then the nearest, the nearest."" Then he said: ""Who is this with you, O Abu Rimthah?"" I said: My son. He said: ""He shall not offend against you, nor shall you offend against him."" Then I looked, and there was upon the cartilage of his shoulder like the dung of a camel or the egg of a pigeon. I said: Shall I not treat you for this? For I am of a household that practices medicine. He said: ""He who placed it treats it."""
"20207","714 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jubarah ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, 'Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim Abu Maryam narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah al-Taymi, he said: I went with my father toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When I saw him, my father said to me: Do you know who this is? I said: No. He said: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I shuddered when he said that to me, and I used to think the Messenger of Allah was something unlike people; and behold, he was a man with abundant hair with traces of henna in it, and upon him were two green cloaks. So my father greeted him, then they sat conversing for a while. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to my father: ""Is this your son?"" He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. He said: ""Truly?"" He said: Truly, I testify to it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, laughing at the affirmation of my resemblance to my father and at my father's oath over me. Then he said: ""He shall not offend against you, nor shall you offend against him."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: {And no bearer of burdens shall bear the burden of another}. And my father saw like a lump between his shoulders and said: I am among the most skilled of men; shall I not treat it? He said: ""Gently; its physician is He who created it."""
"20208","715 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn Sa'id ibn Abjar narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah, he said: I entered with my father upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and my father saw what was upon his back and said: Let me treat what is upon your back, for I am a physician. He said: ""You are a companion (in kindness); Allah is the Physician."" He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to my father: ""Who is this with you?"" He said: My son; I testify to him for you. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You shall not offend against him, nor shall he offend against you."" And he mentioned that he saw traces of henna upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"20209","716 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, Ibn Abjar narrated to me, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah al-Taymi, he said: I and my father went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was sitting in the courtyard of his house with locks of hair in which there were traces of henna. So his father said to him, and he mentioned similar to it."
"20210","717 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Laqit al-Sadusi, he said: I heard Abu Rimthah say: I came with my father to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""Is this your son?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Do you love him? He shall not offend against you, nor shall you offend against him."""
"20211","718 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (h), he said: And Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, they said: Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to me, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah, he said: I went with my father to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I saw upon his shoulder like an apple. So his father said to him: I am a physician; shall I not lance it? He said: ""Its physician is He who created it."""
"20212","719 - Abu Zur'ah 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah, that he entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a son of his, and he said: ""Is this your son?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""He shall not offend against you, nor shall you offend against him."""
"20213","720 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, (h), and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, (h), and 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, they said: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us, my father Iyad narrated to me, from Abu Rimthah, he said: I went with my father toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When I saw him, my father said: Do you know who this is? I said: No. He said: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I shuddered when I saw that, and I used to think the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was something unlike people; and behold, he was a man with abundant hair with traces of henna in it, and upon him were two green cloaks. So my father greeted him, then they sat and conversed for a while. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to my father: ""Is this your son?"" He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. He said: ""Truly?"" He said: ""I testify to that."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, laughing at the affirmation of my resemblance to my father and at my father's oath over me. Then he said: ""He shall not offend against you, nor shall you offend against him."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: {And no bearer of burdens shall bear the burden of another}. Then my father looked at like a lump between his shoulders and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am among the most skilled of men; shall I treat it? He said: ""No; its physician is He who created it."""
"20214","721 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Muslim said: Musaddad narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: I heard Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah, he said: I entered the mosque with my father, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the shade of the Ka'bah. He said to me: Do you see the man in the shade of the Ka'bah? That is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So a severe trembling seized me. And upon him were two green garments, or two green cloaks, and in him were traces of henna. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Is this your son?"" He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. He said: ""He shall not offend against you, nor shall you offend against him."""
"20215","722 - Al-Walid ibn Hammad al-Ramli narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sa'dan ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Abi 'Imran, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah, he said: I went with my father to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was one with abundant hair with traces of henna in it, upon him two green garments."
"20216","723 - Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Ibrahim, from Sadaqah ibn Abi 'Imran, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah, he said: I and my father went toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When on part of the road, he met us. So my father said: Do you know who this is? I said: No. He said: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And I used to think the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not resemble people. And behold, a man with abundant hair with traces of henna in it, upon him two green cloaks, as if I am looking at the shine of his shins. So he said to my father: ""Who is this with you?"" He said: My son, by Allah, truly. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed at my father's oath over me, then said: ""You have spoken the truth. He shall not offend against you, nor shall you offend against him."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: {And no bearer of burdens shall bear the burden of another}."
"20217","724 - Al-Fadl ibn Harun al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Safwan narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umayr, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah al-Taymi of Taym al-Ribab, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my son. When I saw him, I said to my son: This is the Prophet of Allah. So trembling seized him from him. I said: O Prophet of Allah, I am a physician, and my father was a physician of a household of physicians. So show me your back; if it is a lump I shall lance it, and if it is other than that I shall tell you, for there is no man more knowledgeable of a wound or wounds than I. He said: ""There is no physician but Allah."" And upon him were two green cloaks, and he had hair that grayness had overtaken, and his gray hair was red. So he said: ""Is this your son?"" I said: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. He said: ""Of yourself?"" I said: I testify to it. He said: ""He shall not offend against you, nor shall you offend against him."""
"20218","725 - Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was delivering the khutbah, saying: ""The giving hand is the upper: your mother and your father, then your sister and your brother, then the nearest, the nearest."" Then people of Banu Yarbu' came and said: O Messenger of Allah, these Banu Yarbu' killed so-and-so. He said: ""No soul offends against another."""
"20219","726 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us, Abu Sufyan Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Himyari narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Humrah, from Ghaylan ibn Jami', from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he had hair reaching his shoulders dyed with henna and katam."
"20220","727 - Ibrahim ibn Mattuwayh al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Yaman ibn Sa'id al-Massisi narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Khalifah, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, he said: Abu Rimthah led us in prayer. He said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray, then he gave salam to his right and to his left until we saw the whiteness of his cheeks."
"20221","728 - Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Khalid al-Massisi narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Khalifah, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, he said: An imam of ours, known as Abu Rimthah, led us in 'Asr in our prayer place, and with us was a man who had witnessed the first takbir of the prayer. When Abu Rimthah finished, the man stood to add (a rak'ah). So Abu Rimthah looked and said: I prayed this prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr and 'Umar would stand in the front row to his right. And a man had witnessed the first takbir of the prayer, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, then gave salam to the right and left until we saw the whiteness of his cheeks. Then he turned and faced the people. So the man who had caught the first takbir of the prayer with him stood to add. 'Umar leapt to him and took him by his shoulders and shook him, then said: Sit, for the People of the Book were destroyed only because there was no separation in their prayers. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his sight to him and said: ""Allah has guided you aright, O son of al-Khattab."""
"20222","Those named Yusuf. Yusuf ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Salam. 729 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi al-Haytham al-'Attar narrated to us, Yusuf ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Salam narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Yusuf, seated me in his lap, and wiped over my head."
"20223","730 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi al-Haytham al-'Attar narrated to us, he said: I heard Yusuf ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Salam say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Yusuf."
"20224","731 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Waki' informed us, my father narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi al-Haytham al-'Attar, he said: I heard Yusuf ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Salam say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Yusuf, seated me in his lap, and supplicated for blessing for me."
"20225","732 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya al-Aslami, from Yazid ibn Abi Umayyah al-A'war, from Yusuf ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take a morsel of barley bread and place a date upon it, then say: ""This is the condiment of this."" So he ate it."
"20226","733 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mis'ar, (h), and Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Simsar narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated to us, al-Mu'afa ibn 'Imran narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from al-Nadir ibn Qays, from Yusuf ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Salam, he says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me."
"20227","734 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from al-Nadir ibn Qays, he said: I heard Yusuf ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Salam say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Yusuf."
"20228","735 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, that he heard Yusuf ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Salam say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man and a woman of the Ansar: ""Perform 'umrah in the month of Ramadan, for an 'umrah in it is like a hajj."""
"20229","736 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub narrate, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Musa ibn Sa'd, from Yusuf ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It costs none of you anything to take two garments for Friday besides the garments of his household work."""
"20230","Those named Yasir. Yusayr ibn 'Amr al-Sakuni, a mukhadram (who lived in both pre-Islamic and Islamic times); he settled in Kufah and died there. 737 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Qays ibn Yusayr ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: ""Yusayr ibn 'Amr was a registrar ('arif) in the time of al-Hajjaj."""
"20231","738 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Qays ibn Yusayr ibn 'Amr narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Yusayr ibn 'Amr, he said: ""The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away when I was ten years old."""
"20232","Those named Yahya. Yahya ibn Azhar. As'ad ibn Zurarah al-Ansari. 739 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ghundar informed us, from Shu'bah, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn As'ad ibn Zurarah, he said: I heard Yahya - and I have not met a man among us resembling him - narrate to the people that As'ad ibn Zurarah, the grandfather of Muhammad, was seized by a pain in his throat called dhubhah (quinsy). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I shall surely do my utmost to excuse myself regarding Abu Umamah."" So he cauterized him with his hand, and he died. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What an evil death for the Jews"" - they say: ""Why did he not defend his companion? And I control nothing for him nor for myself from Allah."""
"20233","The musnad of those known by kunyah among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whose names have not been transmitted to us. Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Fihri, it is said his name is al-Harith ibn Hisham. 740 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us with that."
"20234","741 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, 'Affan and Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ya'la ibn 'Ata narrated to us, from Abu Hammam 'Abd Allah ibn Yasar, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Fihri, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Hunayn. We traveled on a hot day of intense heat, and alighted beneath the shade of trees. When the sun declined, I wore my armor and mounted my horse, and went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a tent of his. I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Has the time of departure come? He said: ""Yes."" Then he said: ""O Bilal."" So he sprang from beneath a samurah tree, as if his shadow were the shadow of a bird. He said: At your service and your happiness, and I am your ransom. He said: ""O Bilal, saddle my horse for me."" So he brought out a saddle whose flaps were of palm fiber, with neither pride nor vanity in them. So he saddled, and he mounted, and we mounted. We drew ranks against them that evening and night, and the two cavalries sniffed each other. The Muslims turned fleeing, as Allah said. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger."" Then he plunged upon his horse, took a handful of dust - and the one who was nearer to him than I informed me that he struck their faces with it - and said: ""May the faces be disfigured. So Allah defeated them."" Ya'la ibn 'Ata said: Their sons narrated to me from their fathers that they said: ""None of us remained except his eyes and mouth were filled with dust, and we heard a clatter from the heaven and the earth like the passing of iron over a basin."" And the wording is 'Affan's."
"20235","Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Juhani. 742 - Musa ibn 'Isa ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Yazani, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Juhani, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), two riders appeared. When he saw them, he said: ""Two Kindis, two Madhhijis."" When they came to him, they were two men of Madhhij. One of them drew near to pledge him. When he took his hand, he said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me: one who saw you and believed in you and affirmed you and followed you, what is for him? He said: ""Glad tidings (Tuba) for him."" He said: Then he wiped over his hand and left."
"20236","743 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn 'Adi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, (h), and 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, (h), and Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, (h), and Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, 'Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, (h), and Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik narrated to us, my father narrated to us, all of them from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Yazani, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I am riding tomorrow to the Jews, so do not greet them first with salam. When they greet you, say: And upon you."""
"20237","744 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, 'Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Yazani, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""We are going tomorrow to the Jews, so do not greet them first with salam. If they greet you, say: And upon you."""
"20238","Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Qayni. That Sariq bought cloth brought by a man who had recited Surah al-Baqarah, and they bargained, and he disappeared from him, then he overtook him. 745 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated to us, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Qayni: that Sariq bought cloth brought by a man who had recited Surah al-Baqarah, and they bargained, and he disappeared from him, then he overtook him. So he brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Sell Sariq."" He said: So I went with him, and the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bargained with me over him for three days, then it occurred to me and I freed him."
"20239","Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, the guardian of 'A'ishah. 746 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Yahya ibn Abi Muhammad, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, the guardian of 'A'ishah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and 'A'ishah in one garment, half of it upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and half upon 'A'ishah."
"20240","Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi. 747 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from 'Uthman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi, from his father, from his grandfather: that Sa'd asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the bequest, and he said: ""For him is the fourth."""
"20241","Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Khatmi al-Ansari. 748 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith and Sa'id ibn 'Amr al-Ash'athi narrated to us, they said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, al-Ju'ayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Khatmi, that he heard Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, while he was asking his father 'Abd al-Rahman: Inform me of what you heard your father narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding gambling. So 'Abd al-Rahman said: I heard my father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever plays with gambling, then stands to pray, his likeness is like one who performs ablution with pus and the blood of a pig. Then it (the prayer) says: Will Allah accept a prayer for him?"""
"20242","Those known as Abu 'Abd Allah. Abu 'Abd Allah al-Ansari al-Khatmi. 749 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Muhammad al-Sulami informed me, from Malih ibn 'Abd Allah al-Khatmi, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Five are among the ways of the Messengers: modesty, forbearance, cupping, the siwak, and perfuming."""
"20243","Those known as Abu Bashir. Abu Bashir al-Ansari. 750 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, (h), and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm, from 'Abbad ibn Tamim: that Abu Bashir al-Ansari informed him that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a messenger. 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr said: I think he said: While the people were in their midday rest: ""There shall not remain upon the neck of a camel a necklace of hair, nor a necklace, except it is cut off."" Malik said: I think that was because of the evil eye."
"20244","751 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Habban ibn Wasi', from his father, from 'Abd Allah ibn Zayd and Abu Bashir al-Ansari: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with them one day, and a woman passed at al-Batha. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to her to go back. So she returned until he prayed, then she passed."
"20245","752 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, my father and my uncle 'Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, they said: My father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib, from the daughter of Abu Bashir, from her father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding fever, he said: ""Cool it with water, for it is from the blast of Hell."""
"20246","Those known as Abu Sabrah. Abu Sabrah al-Ju'fi. 753 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from 'Umayr ibn Sa'id al-Hanafi, from Sabrah ibn Abi Sabrah: that his father came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: ""What are your children?"" He said: 'Abd al-'Uzza, Sabrah, and al-Harith. He said: ""Do not name (him) 'Abd al-'Uzza; name (him) 'Abd Allah, for the best of names are 'Abd Allah, 'Ubayd Allah, al-Harith, and Hammam."" And he supplicated for his children, and they have remained in honor to this day."
"20247","754 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from 'Umayr ibn Sa'id, from Sabrah, from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my son, and he said: ""What are your children?"" I said: So-and-so, so-and-so, and 'Abd al-'Uzza. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of your names are 'Abd Allah, 'Abd al-Rahman, and al-Harith."""
"20248","Abu Sabrah al-Ansari. 755 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, (h), and Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Salamah al-Ansari narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Yazid ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Unays narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Sabrah narrated to me, from his grandfather Abu Sabrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no prayer except with ablution, and no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it. And he does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me, and he has not believed in me who does not recognize the right of the Ansar."""
"20249","Those known as Abu Zuhayr. Abu Zuhayr al-Numayri, his name is Hatim. 756 - 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Subayh ibn Muhriz al-Himsi narrated to us, Abu al-Musabbih al-Maqra'i narrated to us, he said: We would sit with Abu Zuhayr al-Numayri, and he was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would narrate and narrate well. When a man among us supplicated with a supplication, he would say: Seal it with Amin, for Amin in supplication is like the seal upon the scroll. Abu Zuhayr said: And I shall inform you of that: we went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night walking, and came upon a man in a tent persisting in asking. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood listening to him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is incumbent, if he seals."" A man of the people said to him: With what does he seal, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""With Amin; if he seals with Amin, it has become incumbent."" So the man who had asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left and said: Seal, O so-and-so, with Amin, and rejoice."
"20250","757 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (h), and Abu 'Abd al-Malik Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Damdam ibn Zur'ah, from Shurayh ibn 'Ubayd, from Abu Zuhayr al-Numayri: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not kill locusts, for they are the greatest army of Allah."""
"20251","Abu Zuhayr al-Anmari, and it is said Abu al-Azhar. 758 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Yazid ibn Rashid al-Muqri narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, (h), and Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abu Zuhayr al-Anmari, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he took his bed, would say: ""O Allah, forgive me my sin, disgrace Satan, release my pledge, make heavy my scale, and place me in the Highest Company."""
"20252","759 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abu al-Azhar al-Anmari: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he took his bed at night, would say: ""In the name of Allah I have laid my side. O Allah, forgive me my sin, repel my Satan, release my pledge, and make heavy my scale."""
"20253","Those known as Abu 'Amr. Abu 'Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar ibn Makhzum ibn Naqtah ibn Murrah ibn Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy. 760 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from 'Ulayy ibn Rabah, from Nashirah ibn Sumayy, that he heard 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, on the Day of al-Jabiyah, say: ""I have removed Khalid ibn al-Walid and appointed Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah."" So Abu 'Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah stood and said: By Allah, you have removed an agent whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed, sheathed a sword that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had drawn, and laid down a banner that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had tied."
"20254","761 - Abu Husayn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Hamdani al-Kufi the judge narrated to us, Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Yazid, he said: I heard al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Hadrami narrate, from 'Ulayy ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi, from Nashirah ibn Sumayy, he said: I heard 'Umar ibn al-Khattab say on Friday: ""I apologize to you regarding Khalid ibn al-Walid. I ordered him to withhold this wealth for the charity of the Muhajirun, but he gave it to the strong, the eloquent, and the noble. And I have removed him and confirmed Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah."" So Abu 'Amr ibn Hafs said: By Allah, you have not been just. You removed an agent whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed, sheathed a sword that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had drawn, laid down a banner that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had raised, and envied the son of the uncle. So 'Umar said: ""You are near of kin, young in age."""
"20255","Those known as Abu Hatim. Abu Hatim al-Muzani. 762 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (h), and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Jumahi narrated to us, they said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd and Sa'id ibn 'Ubayd, from Abu Hatim al-Muzani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one comes to you whose religion and character please you, marry him (to your daughter). If you do not do so, there will be fitnah (trial) in the land and widespread corruption."" He said it three times."
"20256","Those known as Abu al-Dahdah. Abu al-Dahdah al-Ansari. 763 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has a palm tree, and I am building my wall with it; order him to give it to me so I may build my wall with it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Give it to him for a palm tree in Paradise."" But he refused. So Abu al-Dahdah came to the man and said: Sell me your palm tree for my wall. So he did. Then Abu al-Dahdah came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have bought the palm tree for my wall, so make it his, and I have given it to you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""How many hanging clusters laden (with dates) for Abu al-Dahdah"" - several times. Then Abu al-Dahdah came to his wife and said: O Umm al-Dahdah, go out of the wall, for I have sold it for a palm tree in Paradise. She said: Profitable is the sale - or a word like it."
"20257","764 - Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Humayd al-A'raj, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Abu Mas'ud, he said: When {Who is it that will lend Allah a good loan} was revealed, Abu al-Dahdah said: O Messenger of Allah, does Allah want a loan from us? He said: ""Yes, O Abu al-Dahdah."" He said: Show me your hand. So he extended his hand to him, and he said: I have lent my wall to my Lord, and in my wall are six hundred palm trees. Then he came to the wall and called: O Umm al-Dahdah, while she was in the wall. She said: At your service. He said: Go out, for I have lent it to my Lord."
"20258","765 - Jabrun ibn 'Isa al-Maghribi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jafari al-Maghribi narrated to us, Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father: that Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan levied a military levy upon the people, and they went out, then Abu al-Dahdah returned. So Mu'awiyah said to him: Had you not gone out with the people? He said: Yes, but I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and wished to entrust it to you, fearing I may not meet you: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""O people, whoever among you is entrusted with an affair and bars his door against the needy among the Muslims, Allah will bar him from entering the gate of Paradise. And whoever's concern is this world, Allah will forbid him My companionship, for I was sent with the ruin of this world and was not sent with its building."""
"20259","Those known as Abu Haywah. Abu Haywah, the father of Abu Raja ibn Haywah al-Kindi, a freedman of theirs. 766 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Kharijah ibn Mus'ab, from Raja ibn Haywah, from his father, from his grandfather: that a slave girl from Khaybar passed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while she was pregnant. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whose is she?"" They said: So-and-so's. He said: ""Does he have intercourse with her?"" It was said: Yes. He said: ""Then how will he deal with her child? Will he claim it though it is not his, or will he enslave him while he walks in his hearing and sight? I have intended to curse him with a curse that will enter the grave with him."""
"20260","Those known as Abu al-Nu'man. Abu al-Nu'man al-Azdi. 767 - Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn al-Nu'man, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I saw upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Uhud two coats of mail."
"20261","Those known as Abu Sa'id. Abu Sa'id ibn al-Mu'alla, his name is Rafi'. 768 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn 'Asim, from Abu Sa'id ibn al-Mu'alla, he said: I was praying, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and I did not answer him. When I finished the prayer, he said: ""What prevented you from answering me when I called you? For Allah says: {O you who believe, respond to Allah and to the Messenger when he calls you to that which gives you life}."" Then he said: ""Do not leave the mosque until I teach you a surah of the Qur'an."" He said: So I walked with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he was about to leave the mosque, and I reminded him. He said: ""The Opening of the Book: the seven oft-repeated and the Great Qur'an that I have been given."""
"20262","769 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn 'Asim, from Abu Sa'id ibn al-Mu'alla, he said: I was praying, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me and called me; and he mentioned similar to it."
"20263","770 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me, Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, he said: Marwan ibn 'Uthman informed me that 'Ubayd ibn Hunayn informed him, from Abu Sa'id ibn al-Mu'alla, he said: We used to go to the market in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), passing the mosque and praying in it. One day we passed while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting upon the minbar. I said: Something has happened. So I sat, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: {We have certainly seen the turning of your face toward the heaven} until he finished the verse. I said to my companion: Come, let us bow two rak'ahs before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descends, so we are the first to pray. So we withdrew and prayed them, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended and led the people in Zuhr that day."
"20264","Those known as Abu Sa'd. Abu Sa'd al-Khayr al-Ansari. 771 - Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam say: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amir narrated to me, that Qays ibn al-Harith al-Kindi narrated to al-Walid, that Abu Sa'd al-Ansari narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""My Lord has promised me to admit to Paradise of my ummah seventy thousand without reckoning, and to intercede each thousand for seventy thousand, then my Lord will scoop three scoops with His two hands."" Qays said: So I said to Abu Sa'd: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, with my ear, and my heart retained it. Abu Sa'd said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""That, if Allah wills, will encompass the Muhajirun of my ummah, and Allah will complete it from our Bedouins."""
"20265","772 - 'Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-'Ala narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (h), and 'Umarah ibn Wathimah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, Abu 'Imran 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amir al-Yahsabi narrated to us, it was narrated to him: that Qays ibn al-Harith narrated to them: that Abu Sa'd al-Khayr al-Ansari narrated to them in Qarqisiya: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter, encompassing thereby our Muhajirun, and completing that from a group of our Bedouins."""
"20266","773 - Isma'il ibn Qirat narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Halbas, he said: I went out with Abu Sa'd al-Khayr to buy sacrificial animals, and he pointed to a ram with meat neither high nor low, and said: Buy this, for it resembles the ram of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"20267","774 - And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Halbas, he said: I went out with Abu Sa'd al-Zuraqi; and he mentioned similar to it."
"20268","775 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (h), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Sa'd al-Ansari, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Remorse is repentance, and the repentant from sin is like one with no sin."""
"20269","776 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Sulayman ibn Abi al-Sa'ib, from Firas al-Sha'bani, from Abu Sa'd al-Khayr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Perform ablution from what fire has touched and what pots have boiled."""
"20270","777 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from his father Muhajir ibn Dinar: that Abu Sa'd al-Ansari passed by Marwan ibn al-Hakam on the Day of the House (the siege of 'Uthman) while he was fallen, and Abu Sa'd said: ""Had I known, O son of al-Zarqa, that you were alive, I would have finished you."" So 'Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan bore a grudge for it. When 'Abd al-Malik became caliph, he was brought to him. So Abu Sa'd said: ""Keep regarding me the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" So 'Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan said: ""And what is that?"" He said: He said: ""Preserve (honor) their doers of good and overlook their doers of evil."" And Abu Sa'd was the husband of Asma bint Yazid ibn al-Sakan ibn 'Amr ibn Haram."
"20271","Abu Sa'd ibn Fadalah al-Ansari. 778 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Kawsaj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Ziyad ibn Mina, from Abu Sa'd ibn Fadalah, and he was of the Companions, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When Allah gathers the first and the last on the Day of Resurrection, for a Day about which there is no doubt, a caller will call: Whoever associated in a deed he did for Allah anyone else, let him seek his reward from other than Allah, for Allah is the most free of partners from association."""
"20272","Those known as Abu Khirash. Abu Khirash al-Sulami, and it is said his name is Hadrad. 779 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri al-Ansari narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, from 'Imran ibn Abi Anas: that Abu Khirash al-Sulami narrated to him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever boycotts his brother for a year has shed his blood."""
"20273","780 - Al-Hasan ibn 'Ulayb al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Ufayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, 'Imran ibn Abi Anas narrated to us: that Abu Khirash al-Sulami informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever boycotts his brother for a year is like shedding his blood."""
"20274","781 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, (h), and 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Miqlas al-Misri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub informed me, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, from 'Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Abu Khirash al-Sulami: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The boycotting by a believer of his brother for a year is like shedding his blood."""
"20275","782 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jandal ibn Waliq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Miqlas, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, from 'Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Abu Hadrad al-Aslami, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"20276","Those known as Abu Habib. Abu Habib al-'Anbari, the grandfather of al-Hirmas. 783 - 'Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi and Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi said: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, he said: Al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, al-Hirmas ibn Habib narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his help against a debtor of his. So he said to him: ""Keep to him."" Then he met him after that and said: ""O Abu - brother of - Banu al-'Anbar, what has your captive done?"""
"20277","784 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hudbah ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, al-Hirmas ibn Habib narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a debtor, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Keep to him."" Then he passed him at the end of the day and said: ""O brother of Banu al-'Anbar, what do you intend to do with your captive?"" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was narrating to the people upon the minbar, then he descended to my grandfather, wiped his face, and bestowed upon him a robe."
"20278","Those known as Abu 'Ubaydah. Abu 'Ubaydah al-Du'ali. 785 - Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madini and Muhammad ibn Ruziq ibn Jami' al-Misri said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd al-Mu'adhdhin narrated to us, from Malik ibn 'Ubaydah al-Du'ali, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Were it not for servants of Allah bowing, suckling infants, and grazing cattle, punishment would have been poured upon you in abundance, then ground to powder."""
"20279","Those known as Abu Manfa'ah. Abu Manfa'ah al-Hanafi, the grandfather of Kulayb ibn Manfa'ah. 786 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Murrah al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Kulayb ibn Manfa'ah al-Hanafi, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom shall I honor? He said: ""Your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, and your freedman who follows that - truly a duty, and kinship joined."""
"20280","Those known as Abu Thawr. Abu Thawr al-Fahmi. 787 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (h), and Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (h), and Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn 'Amr al-Ma'afiri, from Abu Thawr al-Fahmi, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a garment of Ma'afiri garments was brought. So Abu Sufyan said: May Allah curse this garment and curse whoever made it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not curse them, for they are from me and I am from them."""
"20281","Those known as Abu Zam'ah. Abu Zam'ah al-Balawi, it is said his name is 'Abd ibn Arqam; he used to reside in Egypt. 788 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughirah narrated to me, from Abu Qays, the freedman of Banu Jumah, he said: I heard Abu Zam'ah al-Balawi, and he was among the Companions of the Tree, pledging the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) beneath it. One day he came to the mosque of al-Fustat and stood in the courtyard, and some severity from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr had reached him. So he said: Do not be severe upon the people, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""A man of Banu Isra'il killed ninety-seven souls, then went to a monk and said: I have killed ninety-seven souls; do you find for me any repentance? He said: No. So he killed the monk. Then he went to another monk and said: I have killed ninety-eight souls; do you find for me any repentance? He said: No. So he killed him. Then he went to a third and said: I have killed ninety-nine souls, among them two monks; do you find for me any repentance? He said: You have done evil; and if I said: Allah is not Forgiving, Merciful, I would have lied. So repent to Allah."" He said: As for me, I shall not leave you after this saying of yours. So he stayed with him on condition of not disobeying him, and would serve him in that. One day a man died with ugly praise over him; when he was buried, he sat upon his grave and wept severely. Then another died with good praise over him; when he was buried, he sat upon his grave and laughed severely. His companions disapproved of that, and gathered to their chief and said: How can this killer of souls shelter with you, having done what you saw? So it entered his mind and their minds. He went to their companion once regarding that, with a companion of his, and spoke to him and said to him: What do you command me? He said: Go and kindle an oven. So he did, then came to him with the news that he had done so. He said: Go and cast yourself into it. The monk became distracted from him, and the other went and cast himself into the oven. Then the monk came to himself and said: I think the man has cast himself into the oven because of my saying to him. So he went to him and found him alive in the oven, sweating. So he took his hand and brought him out of the oven, and said: It is not fitting that you serve me; rather I shall serve you. Inform me of your weeping over the first deceased, and of your laughing over the other. He said: As for the first, when he was buried I saw what he met of evil, so I remembered my sins and wept; and as for the other, I saw what he met of good, so I laughed. And he was thereafter among the great men of Banu Isra'il."""
"20282","Those known as Abu Buhaysah. Abu Buhaysah. 789 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, (h), and Idris ibn Ja'far al-'Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, they said: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan informed us, (h), and 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Bakr ibn Humran narrated to us, Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Sayyar ibn Manzur, from Buhaysah, from her father, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and entered between him and his shirt and embraced him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing whose withholding is not lawful? He said: ""Water."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing whose withholding is not lawful? He said: ""Salt."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing whose withholding is not lawful? He said: ""If you do good, it is good for you."""
"20283","Those known as Abu Shaybah. Abu Shaybah al-Khudri, the brother of Abu Sa'id. 790 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Yunus ibn al-Harith, Abu Musarrih - or Mishras - narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Shaybah al-Khudri say: Abu Shaybah al-Khudri informed us: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, will enter Paradise."""
"20284","Abu Sa'id al-Ansari al-Zuraqi. 791 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Fayd, from 'Abd Allah ibn Murrah, from Abu Sa'id, that a man of Ashja' asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have a wife who is nursing, and I dislike that she become pregnant; shall I practice 'azl (coitus interruptus) with her? He said: ""What is decreed in the womb will surely be."""
"20285","Those known as Abu Burdah. Abu Burdah, the brother of Abu Musa al-Ash'ari ibn Qays. 792 - Hafs ibn 'Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, 'Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, (h), and 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us, they said: 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, 'Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, Kurayb ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Abu Musa, from Abu Burdah ibn Qays, the brother of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, make the passing of my ummah by spearing and plague."""
"20286","793 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to me, he said: 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, 'Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Kurayb ibn al-Harith ibn Abi Musa, from Abu Burdah ibn Qays, the brother of Abu Musa: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, make the slaying of my ummah in Your path by spearing and plague."""
"20287","Abu Burdah al-Ansari, then al-Zafari. 794 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn al-Harith, he said: Abu Sakhr Humayd ibn Ziyad informed me, from 'Abd Allah ibn Mughith ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There will emerge from al-Kahinan a man who studies the Qur'an with a study none shall study after him."""
"20288","Those known as Abu Tarif. Abu Tarif al-Hudhali. 795 - 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Sumayrah, from Abu Tarif, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he besieged al-Ta'if, and he would lead us in 'Asr prayer early, such that if a man shot (an arrow) he would see the sites of his arrows."
"20289","796 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Sumayrah, Abu Tarif narrated to me: that he witnessed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was besieging the people of al-Ta'if, and he would lead us in 'Asr prayer early, such that if a man shot his arrows he would see the sites of the arrows."
"20290","Those known as Abu Qutaylah. Abu Qutaylah, and there is disagreement over his companionship. 797 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawwazi narrated to us, Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to me, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abu Qutaylah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among the people in the Farewell Hajj and said: ""There is no prophet after me and no ummah after you. So worship your Lord, establish your five, fast your month, and obey your rulers; you will enter the Paradise of your Lord."""
"20291","Those known as Abu 'Aqrab. Abu 'Aqrab, and his name is Muslim. 798 - Al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, from Abu Nawfal ibn Abi 'Aqrab, from his father, he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting? He said: ""Fast a day of the month."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am stronger. He said: ""Fast two days of the month."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, increase me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Increase me, increase me; fast three days of every month."""
"20292","Those known as Abu 'Amir. Abu 'Amir, unattributed. 799 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal informed us, from 'Ali ibn Mudrik, from Abu 'Amir, that there was something among them and he stayed back from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""What held you back?"" He said: I read this verse: {O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; those astray will not harm you when you are guided}. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Those astray among the disbelievers will not harm you when you are guided."""
"20293","Abu 'Amir al-Sakuni. 800 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from 'Utbah ibn Humayd, from 'Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu 'Amir al-Sakuni, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the perfection of righteousness? He said: ""That you do in secret the deed of the open."""
"20294","Those known as Abu Khalid. Abu Khalid al-Sulami, he used to reside in al-Haram. 801 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, (h), and Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Malih narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Khalid, from his father, from his grandfather, and he had companionship with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When a station from Allah precedes for a servant that he does not reach by his deeds, Allah tests him in his body, his wealth, and his child, then grants him patience over that until he reaches the station that preceded for him from Allah, Mighty and Exalted."""
"20295","802 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-'Askari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Hafs al-Nufayli narrated to us, Abu al-Malih narrated to us, a man of Banu Sulaym called Muhammad ibn Khalid narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, and he had companionship, that he went out visiting a brother of his, and before reaching him it reached him that he was ill. So he said: I have come to you visiting, and I have come to you visiting the sick and bringing glad tidings. He said: How have you combined all this? He said: I went out intending to visit you, and your illness reached me, so it became a sick visit; and I bring you glad tidings with something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and he mentioned similar to the hadith of al-Nufayli."
"20296","Those known as Abu Hind. Abu Hind al-Dari. 803 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, he said: Abu Sakhr informed me that Makhul narrated to him that Abu Hind narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever stands a stand of showing off and seeking repute, Allah will show him off and expose him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"20297","804 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Abu Sakhr Humayd ibn Ziyad narrated to me, from Makhul, he said: I heard Abu Hind al-Dari say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever stands a stand of showing off, Allah will show him off; and whoever stands a stand of seeking repute, Allah will expose him."""
"20298","805 - Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Baqi al-Massisi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ziyad ibn Fa'id ibn Ziyad ibn Abi Hind al-Dari narrated to me, my father Ziyad ibn Fa'id narrated to me, from his father Fa'id ibn Ziyad, from his grandfather Ziyad ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Hind al-Dari, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever shows off with Allah for other than Allah has absolved himself from Allah."""
"20299","806 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-'Asqalani narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ziyad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Ziyad, from his father Abu Hind al-Dari, that they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as six men: Tamim ibn Aws ibn Kharijah ibn Sawdan ibn Judhaymah ibn Dira' ibn 'Adi ibn al-Dar, his brother Nu'aym ibn Aws, Yazid ibn Qays, Abu Hind ibn 'Abd Allah, his brother al-Tayyib ibn 'Abd Allah - whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named 'Abd al-Rahman - and Fakih ibn al-Nu'man. So they embraced Islam and asked him to grant them land of the land of Sham. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Ask wherever you like."" So they rose from him consulting over a place to ask him for. Tamim said: I think we ask him for Bayt al-Maqdis and its district. Abu Hind said: Do you see the kingdom of the Persians today - is it not in Bayt al-Maqdis? Tamim said: Yes."
"20300","807 - Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Baqi al-Massisi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ziyad narrated to me, my father Ziyad ibn Fa'id narrated to me, from his father Fa'id ibn Ziyad, from his grandfather Ziyad ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Hind al-Dari, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: ""Whoever is not pleased with My decree and patient over My trial, let him seek a lord besides Me."""
"20301","Abu Hind the cupper. 808 - Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us, Ibn Aishah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Banu Bayadah, give (your women) in marriage to Abu Hind and accept marriage from him."
"20302","Those called Abu Fatimah. Abu Fatimah al-Damri. 809 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala al-Himsi narrated to us, my grandfather Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban, from his father, from Makhul, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Abu Fatimah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, command me a deed that I may hold to and act upon. He said: Upon you is jihad in the path of Allah, for there is nothing like it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that I may hold to and act upon. He said: Upon you is emigration, for there is nothing like it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that I may hold to and act upon. He said: Upon you is prostration, for you do not prostrate a single prostration to Allah except that Allah raises you a degree thereby and removes a sin thereby."
"20303","810 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kathir ibn Murrah: that Abu Fatimah narrated to them, saying: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of a deed we may hold to and act upon. He said: Upon you is emigration, for there is nothing like it. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform us of a deed we may hold to and act upon. He said: Upon you is jihad, for there is nothing like it. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform us of a deed we may hold to and act upon. He said: Upon you is fasting, for there is nothing like it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform us of a deed we may hold to and act upon. He said: Upon you is prostration, for you do not prostrate a single prostration to Allah except that Allah raises you a degree thereby and removes a sin from you thereby."
"20304","811 - Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Hadrami, from Kathir ibn Murrah who said: I heard Abu Fatimah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make abundant prostration, for there is no servant who prostrates a single prostration to Allah except that Allah raises him a degree thereby."
"20305","812 - al-Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Amr al-Maafiri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abu Fatimah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Fatimah, if you wish to meet me, then make abundant prostration."
"20306","813 - Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd informed me, from Muslim, freedman of the family of al-Zubayr, who said: I visited Abd Allah ibn Iyas ibn Abi Fatimah al-Damri and he narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he turned to us and said: Who among you would love to wake up in the morning never falling ill? So we hastened to answer him, saying: We would, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then we recognized it (displeasure) in his face, and he said: Would you love to be like braying donkeys? They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Would you not love to be people of trial and people of expiations? For by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, Allah indeed tests the believer with trial, and He does not test him thereby except out of His honor for him. Allah has assigned him a station which he has not reached by any of his deeds, so He tests him with such trial as will bring him to that rank."
"20307","814 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to me, from Muslim Abu Aqil, freedman of al-Zubayr, from Abd Allah ibn Iyas ibn Abi Fatimah, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same likewise."
"20308","815 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami al-Misri narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir al-Sarhi narrated to us, Rushdyn ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zuhrah ibn Mabad, from Abd Allah ibn Unays ibn Abi Fatimah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"20309","Those called Abu Taliq. Abu Taliq al-Ashjai. 816 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Talq ibn Habib, from Abu Taliq: that his wife said to him, while he owned a camel and a she-camel: Give me your camel so I may perform Hajj on it. He said: It is held back (as endowment) in the path of Allah. She said: It is indeed in the path of Allah that I perform Hajj on it. She said: Then give me the she-camel and perform Hajj on your camel. He said: I do not prefer anyone over myself. She said: Then give me from your provision. He said: I have nothing extra beyond what I take with me and what I leave for you, and had I anything with me I would have given you. She said: Since you have done what you have done, then convey my greeting to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when you meet him and tell him what I said to you. When he met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he conveyed her greeting of peace to him and informed him of what she had said to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umm Taliq spoke the truth. Had you given her your camel it would have been in the path of Allah, and had you given her your she-camel it would have been in the path of Allah, and had you given her from your provision Allah would have replaced it for you. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, then what equals Hajj? He said: An Umrah in Ramadan."
"20310","Those called Abu al-Fil. Abu al-Fil al-Khuzai. 817 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Dawlabi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb who said: Abd Allah ibn Jubayr al-Khuzai narrated to me, from Abu al-Fil, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile him, meaning Maiz ibn Malik."
"20311","Those called Abu Habbah. Abu Habbah al-Badri, and he is Abu Habbah ibn Amr ibn Thabit, one of Banu Thalabah ibn Amr ibn Awf. 818 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah: concerning the naming of those among the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then among Banu Thalabah ibn Amr ibn Awf: Abu Habbah."
"20312","819 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: concerning the naming of those among the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then among Banu Thalabah ibn Amr ibn Awf: Abu Habbah ibn Amr ibn Thabit."
"20313","820 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, freedman of Uthman, that he heard Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman report that he heard Abu Habbah give fatwa to the people that there is no harm in what a man throws of pebbles at the Jamarat in terms of number. Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman said: So I mentioned that to Abd Allah ibn Amr and he said: Abu Habbah spoke the truth, and Abu Habbah was a Badri."
"20314","What Abu Habbah transmitted. 821 - Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab who said: Ibn Hazm informed me: that Ibn Abbas and Abu Habbah al-Ansari said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was taken up (in the Ascension) until I appeared at a level where I could hear the scratching of the pens."
"20315","822 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uzayz narrated to us, Salamah ibn Rawh narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab: Ibn Hazm informed me, that Ibn Abbas and Abu Habbah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then I was taken up until I appeared at a level where I could hear the scratching of the pens."
"20316","823 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Rabiah Fahd ibn Awf narrated to us; (ha) and Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Surah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; (ha) and Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Abu Habbah al-Badri who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Ubayy ibn Kab he said: Gabriel has commanded me to recite to you: Those who disbelieved. Ubayy said: O Messenger of Allah, have I then been mentioned there? He said: Yes. He said: So he wept."
"20317","824 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami al-Misri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Dayf narrated to us, Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Abu Habbah al-Badri who said: On the day of Hunayn the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would look in no direction except that he saw Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith fighting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abu Sufyan is the best of my family, or among the best of my family."
"20318","Those called Abu al-Mualla. Abu al-Mualla al-Ansari. 825 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ibn Abi al-Mualla, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon and said: A man whose Lord gave him the choice between living in this world as long as he wishes to live of it, eating of it, and meeting his Lord, and he chose meeting his Lord. Abu Bakr wept. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you not amazed at this old man? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a righteous man whom his Lord gave the choice between this world and meeting his Lord, and he chose meeting his Lord. Abu Bakr was the most knowledgeable of them of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said, and Abu Bakr said: We would ransom you, O Messenger of Allah, with our wealth and our children. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none among the people more beneficent to us in his companionship and his wealth than Ibn Abi Quhafah. Had I taken a close friend (khalil) I would have taken Ibn Abi Quhafah, but rather affection and the brotherhood of faith; and your Companion is the close friend of Allah."
"20319","Those called Abu al-Shumus. Abu al-Shumus al-Balawi. 826 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr Abu Jafar al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Bakr ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; (ha) and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, saying: Ziyad ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Sulaym ibn Mutayr, from his father, from Abu al-Shumus al-Balawi: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade his Companions on the day of al-Hijr (the rocky land of Thamud) from (using) their well; so the one with dough threw away his dough and the one with hays threw away his hays."
"20320","Those called Abu Ghazziyah. Abu Ghazziyah al-Ansari. 827 - Muhammad ibn Abdah al-Missisi narrated to us, Abu Tawbah al-Rabi ibn Nafi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Ghazziyah, from Abu Ghazziyah al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not combine my name and my kunyah."
"20321","Those called Abu Sirmah. Abu Sirmah al-Ansari. 828 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hayyan, from Lulujah, from Abu Sirmah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: O Allah, I ask You my sufficiency and the sufficiency of my freedman."
"20322","829 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hayyan, from Lulujah, from Abu Sirmah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever harms, Allah will harm him, and whoever causes hardship, Allah will cause hardship upon him."
"20323","830 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, saying: al-Qanabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hayyan, from Lulujah, from Abu Sirmah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever harms, Allah will harm him, and whoever splits (opposes and causes dissension), Allah will split upon him."
"20324","831 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hayyan, from Ibn Muhayriz al-Shami, that he heard Abu Said al-Khudri and Abu Sirmah al-Ansari say: We took captives in the raid of Banu al-Mustaliq, the same raid in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gained Juwayriyah bint al-Harith. Some of us wanted to take wives and some of us wanted to enjoy and then sell. So we discussed withdrawal (azl) among ourselves and mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: It does not matter if you do not practice withdrawal, for Allah has decreed whatever He will create until the Day of Resurrection."
"20325","Those called Abu Maryam. Abu Maryam al-Azdi, who used to reside in Syria in Palestine. 832 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us; (ha) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, saying: Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us; (ha) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abu Maryam, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is put in charge of any affair of the Muslims and then veils himself from their need, poverty and want, Allah will veil Himself on the Day of Resurrection from his need, want, poverty and necessity."
"20326","Abu Maryam al-Ghassani, grandfather of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, who used to reside in Hims. Ahmad ibn Hanbal said: His name is Amr ibn Murrah. 833 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us; (ha) and Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariya al-Araj narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us; (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi narrated to us, saying: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Maryam al-Ghassani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he handed me the standard, and I shot pebbles before him, which pleased him, and he supplicated for me."
"20327","834 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Ala, of the family of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: A girl was born to me tonight. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And tonight Surah Maryam was revealed to me. Name her Maryam. So she used to be called Maryam."
"20328","835 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us; (ha) and Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariya al-Iyadi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Hujr ibn Hujr, from Abu Maryam who said: A Bedouin came until he reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting with a crowd of people around him, and said: Will you not give me something I may learn and carry and which benefits me and does not harm you? The people said: Quiet, sit down. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, for the man only asked in order to learn. He said: So they made room for him until he sat down. He said: What was the first matter of your prophethood? He said: Allah took the covenant from me just as He took their covenant from the Prophets, then he recited: And when We took from the Prophets their covenant, and from you, and from Nuh and Ibrahim and Musa and Isa son of Maryam, and We took from them a solemn covenant. And the Messiah son of Maryam gave glad tidings of me, and the mother of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw in her dream that a lamp came out from between her legs by which the palaces of Syria were lit. The Bedouin said: Hah, and he drew his head nearer, for there was something (deafness) in his hearing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And beyond that."
"20329","836 - Uthman ibn Khalid al-Salafi al-Himsi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Khabairi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Hujr, from Abu Maryam: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the dabb (spiny-tailed lizard)."
"20330","Those called Abu Las. Abu Las al-Khuzai, and his name is Muhammad ibn al-Aswad. 837 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; (ha) and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, from Abu Las al-Khuzai who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried us on some weak camels of the sadaqah camels for Hajj. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we do not think these will carry us. He said: There is no camel except that upon its hump is a devil, so when you ride them, mention the blessing of Allah upon you as Allah commanded you, then subdue them for yourselves, for it is only Allah who carries."
"20331","838 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, from Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, from Abu Las al-Khuzai, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"20332","Those called Abu Sakinah. Abu Sakinah, not traced to a lineage, and his companionship has been disputed. 839 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: I heard Ali ibn al-Madini say: Abu Sakinah has no known companionship."
"20333","840 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yahya, judge of Rayy, narrated to us, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Sakinah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Honor bread, for Allah has honored it; whoever honors bread, Allah honors him."
"20334","841 - Muhammad ibn Abdah al-Missisi narrated to us, Abu Tawbah al-Rabi ibn Nafi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Bilal ibn Sad who said: I heard Abu Sakinah narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: When one of you owns something worth the price of a slave, let him free it, for each limb of it will ransom a limb of him from the Fire."
"20335","Those called Abu Ubayd. Abu Ubayd, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 842 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; (ha) and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Ubayd, that he cooked a pot for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Hand me a foreleg, for he used to like the foreleg, so I handed him a foreleg. Then he said: Hand me the foreleg, so I handed him the foreleg. He said: Hand me the foreleg. I said: O Prophet of Allah, and how many forelegs does a sheep have? He said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, had you kept silent you would have kept handing me forelegs as long as I asked for them."
"20336","Those called Abu Ruhm. Abu Ruhm al-Samai, also said al-Samai. 843 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah and Abu Zayd al-Hawtiyyan narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us; (ha) and Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Yahya al-Atrabulsi narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Said al-Tujibi, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib who said: Abu al-Khayr Marthad ibn Abd Allah al-Yazani narrated to me, from Abu Ruhm al-Samai who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the worst of thieves is he who steals the tongue of the ruler; among the greatest of sins is he who seizes the wealth of a Muslim man without right; among good deeds is visiting the sick, and part of a complete visit is that you place your hand on him and ask him how he is; among the best of intercessions is that you intercede between two people for marriage until you bring them together; among the garments of the Prophets is the shirt before the trousers; and among what brings answer at supplication is sneezing."
"20337","Abu al-Rudayn. 844 - Abu Muhammad Ibrahim al-Nahwi al-Suri narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu al-Rudayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no people who gather upon the Book of Allah passing it among themselves except that they are guests of Allah, and the angels surround them until they stand or engage in other talk; and no servant sets out seeking knowledge fearing it may die, or copying it fearing it may be effaced, except that he is like one going and returning in the path of Allah; and whoever is held back by his deeds, his lineage will not hasten him forward."
"20338","Those called Abu Suwayd. Abu Suwayd, not traced to a lineage. 845 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to me, from Hatim ibn Abi Nasr al-Qushayri, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Abu Suwayd: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invoked blessings upon those taking the pre-dawn meal (mutasahhirin)."
"20339","Those called Abu al-Mundhir. Abu al-Mundhir. 846 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Yazid ibn Thalab, from Abu al-Mundhir: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has died, so pray over him. Umar said: He is a wicked man, so do not pray over him. The man said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not see the night in which you were guarded in the watch, for he was among them? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and prayed over him, then followed him until when he came to his grave he sat, until when he finished with him he threw three handfuls upon him. Then he said: People praise evil of you and I praise good of you. Umar said: And what is that, O Messenger of Allah? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave us alone from you, O Ibn al-Khattab. Whoever strives in the path of Allah, Paradise has become obligatory for him."
"20340","Those called Abu al-Qayn. Abu al-Qayn al-Aslami. 847 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhui al-Qadi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Said ibn Jumhan, from Abu al-Qayn, that he passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with some dates with him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached out to him to take a handful from it to scatter among his Companions, but he drew the edge of his cloak to his chest and his belly. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: May Allah increase you in stinginess."
"20341","Those called Abu Kabshah. Abu Kabshah al-Anmari. 848 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, that Azhar narrated to him, from Abu Kabshah, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting, a woman passed by him, so he stood up (and went) to his family. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us dripping. We said: O Messenger of Allah, it is as if something happened. He said: Yes, so-and-so woman passed by me and desire for women fell in my soul, so I went to one of my wives; and do likewise, for among the best of your deeds is coming to the lawful."
"20342","849 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih informed me, Nuaym ibn Ziyad narrated to me, that he heard Abu Kabshah, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks, and their owners are aided in (spending on) them; and the spender on them is like one stretching his hand with charity."
"20343","850 - al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda al-Antaki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan al-Anmari, from Habib ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Kabshah al-Anmari, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like looking at the citron, and he used to like looking at the red pigeon."
"20344","851 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us, from Ismail ibn Awsat, from Muhammad ibn Abi Kabshah, from his father; (ha) and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi and Daran ibn Sufyan al-Basri narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Awsat, from Ibn Abi Kabshah, from his father who said: When it was the raid of Tabuk, some people hastened to al-Hijr to enter it, so it was announced among the people that prayer is gathering. He said: And I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was holding his camel, saying: Why do you enter upon a people with whom Allah is angry? He said: A man called out to him marveling at them: O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of something more marvelous than that? A Messenger of Allah from among yourselves, among you, informing you of what was before you and what will be after you. Be upright and correct, for Allah does not care for your punishment at all."
"20345","852 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us; (ha) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, both from al-Masudi, from Ismail ibn Awsat al-Bajali, from Muhammad ibn Abi Kabshah, from his father who said: When it was the raid of Tabuk, the people hastened to the companions of al-Hijr, entering upon them. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he mentioned the same."
"20346","853 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Abu Amir al-Hawzani, from Abu Kabshah al-Anmari, that he came to a man and said: Lend me your horse, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever lends his horse to a Muslim and the horse leaves dung for him, it will be for him like the reward of seventy horses mounted in the path of Allah; and if it does not leave dung, it will be for him like the reward of a horse mounted in the path of Allah."
"20347","854 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us; (ha) and Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us, saying: And my uncle Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; (ha) and Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Amr ibn Rujbah narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Kabshah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best of you are the best of you to their families."
"20348","855 - Muhammad ibn Fudayl al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Ubadah ibn Muslim al-Fazari narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, from Said Abu al-Buhturi al-Tai: Abu Kabshah al-Anmari narrated to me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I narrate to you a hadith, thrice I swear upon them: no wealth of a servant is decreased by charity; no servant is wronged with a wrong and is patient upon it except that Allah increases him in honor thereby; and no servant opens a door of begging except that a door of poverty is opened for him."
"20349","856 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Missisi narrated to us, Mualla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humran narrated to us, Abu Said Abd Allah ibn Busr narrated to me, from Abu Kabshah al-Anmari who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam was over the left flank and al-Miqdad was over the right flank. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah and the people calmed down, they came with their two horses. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and wiped the dust from their two faces with his garment, and said: I have assigned to the horse two shares and to the rider one share; whoever diminishes them, Allah will diminish him."
"20350","857 - Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Abu Tawbah al-Rabi ibn Nafi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Urwah ibn Ruwaym, from Abu Kabshah al-Anmari who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in one of his raids, and we alighted at a stop and came to him in it. He raised his hands and said: Faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is here, toward Lakhm and Judham."
"20351","858 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, Abu Muayd narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban, from his father, from Abu Kabshah, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to be cupped on the crown of his head and between his shoulders, saying: Whoever spills this blood, it will not harm him to treat himself with anything for anything."
"20352","859 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Kabshah al-Anmari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be cupped on the crown of his head and between his shoulders, and he mentioned the same."
"20353","860 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Kabshah al-Anmari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Ummah are four: a man given wealth who spends it in obedience to Allah, then a man sees him and says: Had I wealth like his I would do with it as he did; so they are equal in reward."
"20354","861 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Kabshah al-Anmari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck the parable of this Ummah as the parable of four persons, and he mentioned similar to it."
"20355","862 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Missisi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Kabshah al-Anmari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck for me the parable of this Ummah as four persons: a man to whom Allah gave knowledge and wealth, so he acts with his knowledge in his wealth; a man to whom Allah gave knowledge but did not give him wealth, so he says: Had Allah given me like what He gave this one I would have acted in it as he acts; so they are equal in reward. And a man to whom Allah gave wealth but did not give him knowledge, so he unleashes it upon its destruction in other than right, neither fearing his Lord in it nor joining kinship in it; and a man to whom Allah gave neither knowledge nor wealth, so he says: Had Allah given me like what He gave this one I would have acted in it as he acts; so they are equal in burden."
"20356","863 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Tubbai narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam al-Arabi narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Kabshah, the same."
"20357","864 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Mufaddal ibn Muhalhil, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Kabshah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"20358","865 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Ibn Abi Kabshah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"20359","866 - Abd Allah ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Madan ibn Abi Talhah, from Thawban, or from Abu Kabshah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Ummah are four: a man to whom Allah gave wealth and he placed it in His path which He ordained, then a man among the Muslims saw him and said: Would that I had wealth like so-and-so so I could act in it as he acts; so they are equal in reward. And a man to whom Allah gave wealth and he placed it in his play, desires and pleasures, then a man saw him and said: Would that I had wealth like so-and-so so I could act in it as he acted; so they are equal in burden."
"20360","867 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Kabshah al-Anmari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of this Ummah is the parable of four: A man to whom Allah gave wealth and knowledge, so he acts with his knowledge, spending it in its right. A man to whom Allah gave knowledge but did not give him wealth, and he says: Had I wealth like this one I would have acted in it as he acts. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are equal in reward. And a man to whom Allah gave wealth but did not give him knowledge, so he squanders his wealth, spending it in other than right. And a man to whom Allah gave neither knowledge nor wealth, and he says: Had I wealth like so-and-so I would have acted in it as he acts. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So they are equal in burden."
"20361","868 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Ubadah ibn Muslim al-Fazari narrated to us, Yunus ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Said Abu al-Buhturi who said: Abu Kabshah al-Anmari narrated to me, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I narrate to you a hadith, so memorize it. The people of this world are but four persons: A servant whom Allah provided wealth and knowledge in it, so he fears his Lord in it, joins his kinship in it, and acts for Allah in it with its right; such is in the best of stations. A servant whom Allah provided knowledge but did not provide him wealth, and he is truthful in intention, saying: Had I wealth I would have acted as so-and-so acts; so their reward is equal. A servant whom Allah provided wealth but did not provide him knowledge, so he stumbles about in his wealth without knowledge, neither fearing his Lord in it, nor joining his kinship in it, nor acting for Allah in it with right; such is in the vilest of stations. And a servant whom Allah provided neither wealth nor knowledge, and he says: Had I wealth I would have acted as so-and-so acts; so it is his intention, and their burden is equal."
"20362","869 - Abu Zurah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Kabshah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it. Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, and he did not place anyone between Salim and Abu Kabshah."
"20363","870 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib al-Taraifi al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Khulayd Utbah ibn Hammad narrated to us, from Said, from Abu Kinanah, from Abu Kabshah al-Anmari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of my Ummah is four persons: A man whom Allah provided wealth, who acts in it in obedience to Allah, then a man sees him and says: Had I wealth like his I would have acted in it as he acted; so they are equal in reward. And a man whom Allah provided wealth and he squandered and ruined it, then a man sees him and says: Had I wealth like his I would have acted in it as he acted; so they are equal in sin."
"20364","Those called Abu Muwayhibah. Abu Muwayhibah, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 871 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Umar ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Riyahi and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, author of al-Maghazi, narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Hubuli, from Ubayd ibn Hunayn, freedman of al-Hakam ibn al-As, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from Abu Muwayhibah, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me by night and said: Abu Muwayhibah, set out, for I have been commanded to seek forgiveness for the people of this Baqi. So I set out, or he said: so we set out. When he reached the middle of al-Baqi he sought forgiveness for the people of the graves, then said: Blessed is for you what you have come to in the morning; if you knew what Allah has saved you from. Trials approach like portions of the dark night, the last of them following the first; the later is worse than the earlier. Then he said: O Abu Muwayhibah, did you know that Allah gave me the choice between His giving me the treasures of the earth and eternity in it, then Paradise, and meeting my Lord? He said: I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, take the keys of the treasures of the earth and eternity in it. He said: No indeed, O Abu Muwayhibah, I have chosen meeting my Lord. Then he sought forgiveness for the people of the graves and left. In the morning his complaint began with which he passed away (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"20365","872 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Ubayd ibn Hunayn, from Abu Muwayhibah, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to pray over the people of al-Baqi, so he prayed over them in his night three times. When it was the third time he said: O Abu Muwayhibah, saddle my mount for me. So I saddled it, and he rode and traveled to the people of al-Baqi, then dismounted and I held his mount, and he stood over them and said: Blessed is for you what you are in compared to what is among the people. Trials have come like portions of the dark night, each riding upon the other; the later is more severe than the earlier. So blessed is for you what you are in. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: O Abu Muwayhibah, I have been given, or he said: I have been given the choice of the keys of what Allah will open upon my Ummah after me, and Paradise, or meeting my Lord. I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, choose for us. He said: I have chosen meeting my Lord. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained only seven or eight (days) until he passed away (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"20366","Those called Abu Salma. Abu Salma, shepherd of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it is said his name is Hurayth. 873 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to me; (ha) and Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Hadhalam al-Dimashqi and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, saying: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir and Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, saying: Abu Sallam narrated to us, saying: Abu Salma, shepherd of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Excellent, excellent, for five, how heavy they are in the Balance: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and glory be to Allah and with His praise; and the righteous child who dies (before) the Muslim man, and he reckons (his reward) with Allah."
"20367","Those called Abu Namlah. Abu Namlah al-Ansari. 874 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri who said: Ibn Abi Namlah al-Ansari informed me: that his father Abu Namlah al-Ansari informed us that while he was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man from the Jews came, and a funeral passed by, and he said: O Muhammad, does this bier speak? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah knows best. The Jew said: It does speak. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever the People of the Book narrate to you, neither confirm them nor deny them, but say: We believe in Allah and His Books and His Messengers; for if it is false you will not have confirmed it, and if it is true you will not have denied it."
"20368","875 - Abu Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani al-Rusafi narrated to us, my grandfather informed us, from al-Zuhri who said: Ibn Abi Namlah al-Ansari informed me, that his father Abu Namlah informed him that while he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man from the Jews came to him and said: O Muhammad, does this bier speak? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah knows best. The Jew said: I bear witness that it speaks. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever the People of the Book narrate to you, neither deny them nor confirm them, but say: We believe in Allah and His Messengers and His Books; for if it is true you will not have denied it, and if it is false you will not have confirmed it."
"20369","876 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed us, from al-Zuhri who said: Namlah ibn Abi Namlah narrated to me, that Abu Namlah al-Ansari narrated to him that while he was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man from the Jews came to him and said: O Muhammad, does this bier speak? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah knows best. The Jew said: I bear witness that it speaks. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever the People of the Book narrate to you, neither confirm them nor deny them, but say: We believe in Allah and His Books and His Messengers; for if it is true you will not have denied it, and if it is false you will not have confirmed it."
"20370","877 - al-Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to me, Muawiyah ibn Yahya al-Sadafi narrated to me, from al-Zuhri who said: Ibn Abi Namlah al-Ansari narrated to me, that his father Abu Namlah al-Ansari informed him that while he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man from the Jews came and said: O Muhammad, does this bier speak? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah knows best. The Jew said: I bear witness that it speaks. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever the People of the Book narrate to you, neither confirm them nor deny them, but say: We believe in Allah and His Books and His Messengers; for if it is true you will not have denied them, and if it is false you will not have confirmed them."
"20371","878 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab: Ibn Abi Namlah al-Ansari narrated to me, that Abu Namlah al-Ansari informed him that while he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man from the Jews came to him and said: Does this bier speak? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah knows best. The Jew said: I bear witness that it speaks. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever the People of the Book narrate to you, neither confirm them nor deny them, but say: We believe in Allah and His Books and His Messengers; for if it is true you will not have denied them, and if it is false you will not have confirmed them."
"20372","879 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uzayz narrated to us, Salamah ibn Rawh narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab: Ibn Abi Namlah narrated to me, that his father informed him that while he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man from the Jews came to him and said: O Muhammad, does this bier speak? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah knows best. The Jew said: I bear witness that it speaks. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever the People of the Book narrate to you, neither confirm them nor deny them, but say: We believe in Allah and His Books and His Messengers; for if it is true you will not have denied them, and if it is false you will not have confirmed them."
"20373","Those called Abu Sayyarah. Abu Sayyarah al-Mutai, and he was a freedman of Banu Bajalah. 880 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq; (ha) and Abu Zurah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, both from Said ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Abu Sayyarah al-Mutai, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have bees. He said: Pay the tenth. I said: And protect its mountain for me; so he protected its mountain for me."
"20374","881 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Said ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Abu Sayyarah al-Mutai who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have bees. He said: Pay the tenth. I said: So protect its mountain for me; so he protected its mountain for me."
"20375","Those called Abu Hadrad. Abu Hadrad al-Aslami. 882 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri; (ha) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Hadrad al-Aslami who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking help for a woman's dower. He said: How much did you fix as her dower? He said: I said: Two hundred dirhams. He said: Had you been scooping from Buthan you would not have increased."
"20376","883 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Hadrad al-Aslami who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he married a woman for a dower of two hundred dirhams, and he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Had you been scooping from Buthan you would not have increased."
"20377","884 - Muhammad ibn Asim al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated to us, Umar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Umar ibn Suhban narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hadrad al-Aslami who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: How much did you fix as dower, O Abu Hadrad? I said: Five awaqi. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you been scooping from Buthan you would not have increased."
"20378","885 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Zakariya, from Abd Allah ibn Said, from his father, from Abu Hadrad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adopt the ways of Mad (live simply), be coarse, and walk barefoot."
"20379","886 - Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Hamd ibn Bashir ibn Abi Hadrad al-Aslami narrated to us, saying: My uncle narrated to me, from Abu Hadrad: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will drive these camels of ours, or who will deliver these camels of ours? A man stood up. He said: What is your name? He said: So-and-so. He said: Sit down. Then another stood up. He said: I will. He said: What is your name? He said: Najiyah. He said: You are for it, so drive it."
"20380","Those called Abu Yazid. Abu Yazid, not traced to a lineage, and the narrators differed, saying: Ibn Yazid, while the correct is Ibn Abi Yazid. 887 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us; (ha) and Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Hakim ibn Abi Yazid, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave people, let some of them benefit from others; and when they seek your advice, advise them."
"20381","888 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Hakim ibn Abi Yazid, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave people, let some of them be provided for by others; and when one seeks advice from his brother, let him advise him."
"20382","889 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; (ha) and Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Hakim ibn Abi Yazid, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave people, let some of them be provided for by others; and when a man seeks advice from a man, let him advise him."
"20383","890 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Hakim ibn Abi Yazid, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave people, let some of them be provided for by others; and when one of you consults his brother, let him advise him."
"20384","891 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Hakim ibn Abi Yazid, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A townsman shall not sell for a Bedouin. Leave people, let some of them benefit from others; and when a man seeks advice from his brother, let him advise him. Thus said Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Hakim ibn Yazid, adding to the narration of the people in this hadith: nor shall a townsman sell for a Bedouin."
"20385","892 - Abd Allah ibn Shabib al-Basri narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Yaqub al-Jazari narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Yazid ibn Abi Hakim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"20386","Those called Abu al-Ramda. Abu al-Ramda al-Balawi. 893 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, that Abu Sulayman, freedman of Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him: that Abu al-Ramda al-Balawi informed him that a man among them drank wine, so he was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and was struck (lashed); then he drank a second time and was brought and he struck him. I do not know whether he said on the third or the fourth (time) he was commanded to be brought and placed upon the cart (?) and his neck was struck (he was executed)."
"20387","Those called Abu al-Zawaid. Abu al-Zawaid al-Yamani. 894 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr Abu Jafar al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Bakr ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Madani narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Nasr narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Matir narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Zawaid who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj, and he addressed the people, saying to them: Do such-and-such and do such-and-such, and avoid such-and-such and avoid such-and-such. Then he would say to them: Have I conveyed? They would say: Yes. Then he would raise his hands and say: O Allah, bear witness; he said it thrice. And I heard him say among what he said: Take the stipend as long as it is a stipend; but when Quraysh contend for kingship among themselves and the stipend becomes a bribe upon your religion, then do not take it."
"20388","Those called Abu al-Sanabil. Abu al-Sanabil ibn Bakak ibn al-Harith ibn Umaylah ibn al-Sabbaq ibn Abd al-Dar ibn Qusayy, of the Muallafah (those whose hearts are reconciled), and his name is Amr, also said Habbah. 895 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Ishaq, with his lineage and name, and that he is of the Muallafah; Amr, and Habbah in my view is a mistake."
"20389","896 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; (ha) and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us; (ha) and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl al-Askari narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abu al-Sanabil ibn Bakak who said: Subayah bint al-Harith gave birth after her husband's death by some twenty-odd nights. When she became free of her postnatal bleeding she adorned herself (for marriage), and that was held against her. Her matter was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If she does so, her term has ended."
"20390","897 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abu al-Sanabil ibn Bakak who said: Subayah gave birth after her husband's death by twenty-three or twenty-five nights. When she became free of her postnatal bleeding she adorned herself, and that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If she does so, her term has become lawful (ended)."
"20391","898 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Attar narrated to us; (ha) and Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abu al-Sanabil ibn Bakak who said: Subayah bint al-Harith gave birth after her husband's death by twenty-three or twenty-five nights. When she rose free of her postnatal bleeding she longed for marriage, and that was disapproved of her or held against her. So I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If she does that, her term has become lawful."
"20392","899 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abu al-Sanabil ibn Bakak who said: Subayah gave birth after her husband's death by twenty-three or twenty-five days. When she became free she longed for husbands, and that was held against her. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: And what prevents her, when her term has indeed ended?"
"20393","900 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from al-Amash and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abu al-Sanabil who said: Subayah gave birth after her husband's death by twenty-three nights. She adorned herself, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached and informed. He said: If she does so, her term has been decreed (ended)."
"20394","Those called Abu Mujibah. Abu Mujibah al-Bahili. 901 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Salil, from Mujibah, from his father or his uncle, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am the man who came to you last year. He said: Why do I see your body emaciated? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have not eaten food by day since I pledged to you. He said: Who commanded you to torment yourself? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am strong. He said: Fast the month of patience (Ramadan) and two days after it. I said: I am strong. He said: Fast the month of patience and three days after it, and fast the sacred months."
"20395","Those called Abu Mutib. Abu Mutib ibn Amr al-Aslami. 902 - Abu Shuayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: A freedman of theirs narrated to me, from Ata ibn Abi Marwan al-Aslami, from Abu Mutib ibn Amr: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) overlooked Khaybar he said to his Companions, and I was among them: Halt. Then he said: O Allah, Lord of the heavens and what they shade, and Lord of the earths and what they carry, and Lord of the devils and what they misguide, and Lord of the winds and what they scatter, I ask You the good of this town and the good of its people, and I seek refuge with You from its evil and the evil of its people and the evil of what is in it. Proceed in the name of Allah. And he used to say it for every town he entered."
"20396","Those called Abu Aminah. Abu Aminah al-Fazari. 903 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Jafar al-Farra who said: I heard Abu Aminah al-Fazari say: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) be cupped."
"20397","904 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, saying: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Jafar al-Farra, from Abu Aminah who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) be cupped."
"20398","Those called Abu Umayyah. Abu Umayyah al-Makhzumi. 905 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us; (ha) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, from Abu al-Mundhir, freedman of Abu Dharr, from Abu Umayyah al-Makhzumi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a thief who confessed a confession, though no goods were found with him. He said: I do not think you stole? He said: Yes indeed. He said: I do not think you stole? He said: Yes indeed. He said: Take him away and cut his hand. He said: So they cut his hand, then they brought him. He said: Seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him. He said: I seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him. He said: O Allah, turn to him in mercy; O Allah, turn to him in mercy."
"20399","Abu Umayyah al-Qushayri, also said al-Damri. 906 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Umayyah who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a journey. When he wanted to eat, I withdrew. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you not take lunch? I said: I am fasting. He said: Shall I not inform you about the traveler? Allah has lifted from him fasting and half of the prayer."
"20400","907 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhajir, from Abu Umayyah al-Damri who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a journey and greeted him. When I went to leave, he said: Wait for lunch, O Abu Umayyah. I said: I am fasting, O Prophet of Allah. He said: I inform you about the traveler: Allah has lifted from him fasting and half of the prayer."
